#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cc-reconcile — the box's one mechanical watcher: board vs reality, the sweep, the wake, the owner's daily line.

  cc-reconcile [repo …]              report the drift, change nothing
  cc-reconcile --apply               fix what has one right answer, stop a runaway, and run the tick (below)
  cc-reconcile --apply --notify      …and hand what needs a person to the repo's session, else the owner (once a day per finding)
  cc-reconcile snapshot [repo …]     print the state snapshot; writes nothing, asks no network
  cc-reconcile view                  the snapshot file as TSV: repo/track · state · waiting_on · why (no rows when stale)
  cc-reconcile sweep [<repo>…|--configured] [--dry]   remove what is finished and forgotten; report what is uncertain
  cc-reconcile digest [--notify]     the whole report: shipped, moving, waiting on you, stopped, cost; --notify posts the phone one
  cc-reconcile investigate [--dry]   the tick's failure investigation, once, by hand; --dry names the cluster it would claim
  cc-reconcile deep-fix [--dry]      the tick's recurring-red investigator, once, by hand; --dry names the case it would claim
  cc-reconcile selfcheck             the decision table and one end-to-end run of each part, no network
    flags: --json · -q · --no-net (never ask GitHub) · --grace SEC (600) · --repeat SEC (86400) · --no-stop

No model is called here. Two things are launched: `cc-audit failure <claim>` (THE INVESTIGATION, below) and one
worker per recurring gate red (THE DEEP FIX, below).

ALIVE: a `claude` whose cwd is the track's worktree, a `cc-loop <repo> <track>`, a live pane in the track's tmux
window, or an `agent` mark (cc-board) naming a window that holds an interactive session for this repo, made less
than 6 h ago, after the start of the last usage-limit episode, and whose seat has taken a turn inside those 6 h
(cc-statusline's per-turn file or the transcript, by the seat's --session-id, or by its cwd when it carries none and
is the one interactive session there; a re-mark is not a turn, and a seat nothing says about — two seats in one cwd
— keeps its clock). Alive with nobody typing for 2 h is `idle`, and neither an idle session nor a bare `agent` mark
moves a `blocked` or `waiting` row back to `running`: those are a session's words, and only work in flight — a
worker, a loop, a pane moved inside 2 h — overrides them. A mark flips a `queued` row and keeps a row off the
abandoned path; it is not work in flight.

WAITING: the worker's own `STATUS: BLOCKED: <question>` line makes a track `waiting` on a person, whatever is
running; a loop sitting out a usage limit waits on the clock and never reaches the owner. Prose is never read.

DRIFT: decidable (the PR merged, a worker is in the worktree, it finished and its PR is open) is applied through
cc-board with a `reconciled:` note. Undecidable (closed PR, gone worktree, refused checkpoint, unpushed branch,
no worker and nothing says why) is reported and, with --notify, offered to the repo's live session through the
broker door (CC_RECONCILE_INJECT, CC_BROKER_SOURCE from the unit); what no session takes pages the owner. A row
that never ran — no claim, never started, no journal, no worktree — is reported as never started, not as lost. A
line about a PR is re-read at GitHub at send time and dropped if the merge ANSWERS it — a safety ask standing
beside it, an unpushed branch, still goes out (--no-net never asks, so never drops). A finished row (`merged`/
`done`) raises nothing on suspicion; a merged row whose branch really holds commits origin lacks is still
reported. A `held` row keeps its fixes, stops, safety asks and its question; the guesses go quiet.
A finished track with an open PR nobody is landing is offered once per PR and alerted once, ever, past the
4 h window — unless the row itself waits on a person, which is somebody having picked it up: that one raises neither.

RUNAWAY: a headless worker with no cc-loop above it is ended on sight; a worker alive with journal, loop log and
worktree untouched for 3 h, seen by two passes, is ended too, never during a usage limit. --no-stop reports only.

SNAPSHOT: an unfiltered run writes ~/.cc/state/reconcile.json; `view` prints it while it is under an hour old.
`snapshot` decides and prints the same and touches no file.

THE TICK (--apply, unfiltered): after the reconcile it runs, in order,
  · cc-trust prune, cc-handoff --sweep --rotate (the reaper, plus — only here, under --apply — handing off a seat
    past the rotate line: its ROTATION), cc-slack approvals-sweep (each its own tool; this gives it a turn)
  · the fixture rule (sweep rule 6) every tick; the full sweep of CC_JANITOR_REPOS once per 24 h
  · the wake, per repo with a board, only while CC_WAKE=on (~/.cc/config) — off by default, the owner's switch
  · the failure investigation (THE INVESTIGATION, below)
  · the digest, once a day after 11:00 America/Los_Angeles (hour and stamp date both in that zone, never the host's),
    stamped but no longer posted — `digest --notify` still posts it by hand

SWEEP (`sweep`): per repo, in order. Rule 1: a `merged`/`done` row past 48 h with a clean worktree and nothing
alive in it → `cc rm`; dirty, alive, or the snapshot disagreeing → reported. Rule 2: a remote track/* branch
whose PR MERGED → deleted on origin (one `gh pr list` per repo, 200 PRs); any other PR state is reported.
Rule 3: a bare tmux window (session main) of a gone or terminal track → killed; `<track>~next` follows its base.
Rule 4: never the planning window, a live pane, or a row that is not terminal. Rule 6 (box-wide): a
`_cc<suite><pid>` fixture whose pid is dead → removed, its windows killed, its handoff-ledger lines dropped;
held by any live process → reported. Rule 9: a `.claude/worktrees/*` subagent worktree silent for 4 h
(CC_JANITOR_AGENT_HOURS) with nothing live in it and no commit its merged PR lacks → removed; else reported.
Anything uncertain is reported, never removed. Log: ~/.cc/state/janitor.log. Repos: CC_JANITOR_REPOS (~/.cc/config).

WAKE (in the tick, CC_WAKE=on only; unset, each repo logs a skip): for each repo whose board is not all `session` rows, that `cc-pause` has not parked and that
has no ~/.cc/state/<repo>/pulse.off (cc-handoff's overlap mark; a person may touch it too), the seat is woken when a queued row could start now (`cc-brief ready`, the one network call, skipped under --no-net)
or a row is `blocked`, and that same state was not already sent inside 24 h — one look string per half, so a queued
row's verdict changing does not re-announce a row that has been blocked all along
(a queued row inside a live bundle — cc-bundle's `bundle: <row>` mark, the bundle row live — is in flight and never offered)
(~/.cc/state/<repo>/pulse.look). `cc-tier allows pulse` / `start` gate it. Waking is `cc <repo>` when tmux
session main has no live `<repo>` window, else one `cc-msg` line — never while the pane shows a turn in progress
or a usage-limit line, never mid-handoff before the cutover (after it, the successor is the live seat). Orchs (`<repo>@<alias>`) are never woken. Log: ~/.cc/state/pulse.log.

DIGEST (`digest`): the five questions off the boards and the snapshot — shipped in the last day, moving (a queued
row inside a live bundle is counted "in bundles", not queued: the bundle row is what is moving), waiting
on you (each row's question, then the owner's 📌 pins from ~/.cc/slack/revisit.json), stopped, cost (cc-spend
today) — and one line from the failure ledger, what it holds and what crossed the rule (cc-failures owns the numbers;
an empty ledger is no line). That whole report is what `digest` prints. What `--notify` POSTS (the tick itself no
longer does — it only stamps the day) is the phone one: the counts line, the limit and the tier's word,
how many failure kinds crossed the rule (none is no line), every waiting row's question (cut to 120) and the asks count,
then one line naming what it left out, linked to CC_DIGEST_LINK (~/.cc/config, an https URL; anything else reads "the
Home tab"). `--notify` prints what it posts.

THE INVESTIGATION rides the tick (docs/design-failure-noticing-2026-09-11.md, The investigation) and has no timer of
its own. Each tick, if ~/.cc/config has CC_FAILURES_INVESTIGATE=on (the owner's setting; absent, it is inert), `cc-tier
allows explore` says yes, and no `cc-audit failure` is running anywhere on the box, the pass takes ONE eligible
cluster with `cc-failures claim` and launches `cc-audit failure <claim>` as a transient user unit that outlives this
oneshot (a detached child where there is no user manager), one line in reconcile.log. The tier saying no claims
nothing: the cluster stays eligible and unclaimed with its age, and the run prints that the tier holds it. Nothing here
reads the report, opens a row or posts: cc-audit delivers. `investigate --dry` claims and launches nothing and names
the cluster the pass would take and what holds it. CC_RECONCILE_LAUNCH=CMD (tests) runs `CMD failure <claim>` in
place of the unit and skips the box-wide running scan unless CC_RECONCILE_PROC names a fixture /proc.

THE DEEP FIX rides the same tick. A gate case that goes red on landing after landing is not bought again by every PR
it blocks: once `cc-failures recurring` counts it red on CC_RECURRING_RED_MIN landings (3) inside
CC_RECURRING_RED_WINDOW_H hours (72), and ~/.cc/config has CC_RECURRING_RED_FIX=on (absent, inert) and `cc-tier allows
explore` says yes (no answer holds, as above), the pass takes ONE case with `cc-failures recurring claim` and launches
ONE worker on it: `cc <scope> recurring-red-<case> --go <brief> --model claude-opus-5-5 --effort max`. The worker
finds the cause and lands its fix through the lane like any PR, or files a raised- row when the cause is outside the
repo. The claim holds the case for CC_RECURRING_RED_COOL_H hours (24) and while its worker's journal has no STATUS
line; after that the case is taken again only when it has gone red on the threshold again since the claim, and two
claims a rolling day is the cap. While a claim holds, the landing does not re-run the gates of a PR whose red is only
that case (`cc-failures recurring held`). The thresholds are cc-config keys. CC_RECONCILE_DEEP_LAUNCH=CMD (tests)
runs CMD in place of `cc`.

A NAG THE STATE DISPROVES IS A FAILURE, WRITTEN HERE (the design's writers table: "cc-reconcile (a nag the
authoritative state disproved)"). Every nag the --notify pass sends — the session's "review and land it", the owner's
⏳ page, the ask about a worktree the board never heard of — is a memo in the seen-ledger with its time. When a memo
drops, the pass holds it against the authoritative state AT THAT TIME: a landing cc-land already had (its queue log,
its work record's `first`), a PR merged or opened before the nag. One the state disproves is one `cc-failures record`
line, notification/false-action-needed, at the nag's own time, naming the PR; one that simply cleared is nothing, and
so is one GitHub could not be asked about. The writer never changes the pass: see false_nags() and record_failure().

Exit: 0 the board matches reality · 1 something needs a person · 2 usage error.
"""
import calendar, datetime, glob, json, os, re, shutil, signal, subprocess, sys, time, zoneinfo

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
BIN = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))      # siblings come from the same bin/ as this copy
BOARDS, WTS, STATE, DEV = f"{HOME}/.cc/boards", f"{HOME}/.cc/worktrees", f"{HOME}/.cc/state", f"{HOME}/dev"
PROJECTS = f"{HOME}/.claude/projects"                # transcripts, one directory per cwd (path with / and . as -)
GRACE = 600        # a track the board touched less than this ago is left alone: claude takes a moment to appear
REPEAT = 86400     # a finding that persists is worth one push a day
PRMAX = 40         # PR lookups per run
ORPHANPRS = 10     # branch→PR lookups orphans() makes
WEDGED = 3 * 3600  # a worker alive with nothing moved for this long is stuck (cc-loop caps an iteration at 1 h)
IDLE = 2 * 3600    # a live pane with nobody typing at it for this long is idle, not running
AGENT_MARK = 6 * 3600   # an `agent` mark holds a row this long
WEDGE_SEEN = 5400  # …and a wedge counts only if the previous run saw it too
PENDING = 14400    # finished with an open PR for this long and nobody landing it: the owner hears
BETWEEN_ROUNDS = 1800   # a landing record younger than this is a landing between rounds, not abandoned
TERMINAL = ("merged", "done")
FRESH = 3600       # a snapshot older than this decides nothing
QUEUED = ("queued", "todo")   # both words are read; `queued` is the one written
STALE = 48 * 3600  # sweep rule 1: a terminal track younger than this is still being looked at
SWEEP_PRS = 200    # sweep rule 2: one `gh pr list` per repo, capped
NEXT = "~next"     # cc-handoff's successor window suffix
AGENT_WT = ".claude/worktrees"   # sweep rule 9: where the harness puts a subagent's worktree
AGENT_HOURS = 4    # …and the silence that says its subagent is gone (CC_JANITOR_AGENT_HOURS)
QUIET_H = 24       # wake: hours the same look is not sent again
WORKING_FOOTER = "esc to interrupt"   # the pane footer for a turn in progress (the string cc-slack reads)
BOARD_DUE = ("queued", "blocked", "todo")
PULSE_LOG, JANITOR_LOG = f"{STATE}/pulse.log", f"{STATE}/janitor.log"
DIGEST_HOUR, DIGEST_TZ = 11, "America/Los_Angeles"   # the owner's late morning, as the cc-digest.timer it replaces said


def now():
    return time.time()


def epoch(ts):
    """Board timestamps are UTC '2026-08-30T21:01:43Z'; anything else is 'long ago', never 'in the future'."""
    try:
        return float(calendar.timegm(time.strptime(str(ts), "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")))
    except Exception:
        return 0.0


def stamp(t=None):
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(t))


def sh(*cmd, timeout=120, cwd=None):
    """Run a command; None when it could not be run or hung. A timer job never dies of one tool."""
    try:
        return subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, cwd=cwd, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except Exception:
        return None


def sib(name):
    """A sibling tool: from CC_RECONCILE_STUBS when a selfcheck stands one in, else beside this copy."""
    d = os.environ.get("CC_RECONCILE_STUBS")
    return f"{d}/{name}" if d and os.path.exists(f"{d}/{name}") else f"{BIN}/{name}"


def setting(key, default=""):
    """A ~/.cc/config value through cc-config, the file's one reader: the environment wins."""
    p = sh(sib("cc-config"), "get", key, default, timeout=20)
    return p.stdout.strip() if p is not None else os.environ.get(key, default)


def mark_why(t, wins, repo, t0, mark, started=0.0, advanced=None):
    """The `agent` mark weighed: (holds?, why not). The window must hold a session for THIS repo (`<repo>` or
    `<repo>@<alias>`); the mark goes cold at `mark` seconds, and at once if made at or before a lifted limit's start
    (the subagent holding it died on the 429; the box works on through the episode, so a later mark is alive).
    `advanced` is when the seat in that window last took a turn (seat_turn), None when nothing says: a seat that
    has not taken a turn for `mark` seconds holds nothing, however fresh the mark — a session's detached re-mark
    loop refreshes `agent_at` on a liveness poll alone, which a stalled seat passes (an orch seat sat a day on a
    row it kept marked, raised 2026-09-17). The brief: "a mark whose seat has not advanced expires"."""
    ag = (t.get("agent") or "").strip()
    win = wins.get(ag) or ""
    if not ag or not (win == repo or win.startswith(repo + "@")):
        return False, ""
    at = epoch(t.get("agent_at"))
    if not at:
        return False, "marked by a live session, but the mark carries no time"
    if t0 - at >= mark:
        return False, f"marked by a live session {(t0 - at) / 3600:.0f} h ago, mark expired"
    if started and at <= started:
        return False, ("marked before the usage limit that began at "
                       + time.strftime("%H:%MZ", time.gmtime(started)) + " — that subagent died with it")
    if advanced is not None and t0 - advanced >= mark:
        return False, (f"marked by a live session, but that seat has not taken a turn for "
                       f"{(t0 - advanced) / 3600:.0f} h — a re-mark is not a turn, mark expired")
    return True, ""


def window_panes():
    """{"<window id>:<server pid>": pane pid} for every tmux pane, the key a mark carries (cc-board agent_id)."""
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["tmux", "list-panes", "-a", "-F", "#{window_id}:#{pid}\t#{pane_pid}"],
                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
    except Exception:
        return {}
    wp = {}
    for ln in out.stdout.splitlines():
        f = ln.split("\t")
        if len(f) == 2 and f[0].strip() and f[1].strip().isdigit():
            wp.setdefault(f[0].strip(), f[1].strip())
    return wp


def seat_turn(pane_pid):
    """When the session in that pane last took a turn (epoch), or None when nothing says. The seat is the `claude`
    under the pane's shell. Its id is the `--session-id` on its command line, and the turn is the newer of
    cc-statusline's per-turn file (~/.cc/state/statusline/<id>.json, CC_STATUSLINE_DIR) and the transcript
    (~/.claude/projects/*/<id>.jsonl). Only a cc-handoff successor carries an id; `cc <repo>` and `cc --orch` start
    the seats that mark rows with none (review of #538), so a seat with no id is known by its cwd — the newest
    transcript in that cwd's directory and the newest per-turn file whose raw.cwd is that cwd — and only while it is
    the ONE interactive `claude` on the box in that cwd: two peers in one checkout (a main seat and an orch) say
    nothing about each other, so both are None (cc-context's own rule). A stalled turn writes neither file, and
    None is no evidence, so that mark keeps the clock it has."""
    if not pane_pid:
        return None
    todo, seen, seat, sid = [str(pane_pid)], set(), "", ""
    while todo and not seat:
        pid = todo.pop()
        if pid in seen:
            continue
        seen.add(pid)
        try:
            kids = open(f"/proc/{pid}/task/{pid}/children").read().split()
        except OSError:
            kids = []
        for k in kids:
            try:
                if open(f"/proc/{k}/comm").read().strip() != "claude":
                    todo.append(k)
                    continue
                argv = open(f"/proc/{k}/cmdline", "rb").read().decode("utf-8", "replace").split("\0")
            except OSError:
                continue
            seat = k
            i = argv.index("--session-id") if "--session-id" in argv else -1
            if 0 <= i < len(argv) - 1 and re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*", argv[i + 1]):
                sid = argv[i + 1]
            break
    if not seat:
        return None
    sl = os.environ.get("CC_STATUSLINE_DIR") or f"{STATE}/statusline"
    if sid:
        paths = [f"{sl}/{sid}.json"] + glob.glob(f"{PROJECTS}/*/{sid}.jsonl")
    else:                                               # no id: the seat is its cwd, if it is alone there
        try:
            cwd = os.path.realpath(os.readlink(f"/proc/{seat}/cwd"))
        except OSError:
            return None
        if len(interactive_in(cwd)) != 1:
            return None
        paths = glob.glob(f"{PROJECTS}/{re.sub(r'[/.]', '-', cwd)}/*.jsonl")
        for path in sorted(glob.glob(f"{sl}/*.json"), key=mtime, reverse=True):
            try:                                        # newest first: the first whose cwd matches is the one
                raw = json.load(open(path)).get("raw") or {}
            except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):
                continue
            if os.path.realpath(raw.get("cwd") or "/nonexistent") == cwd:
                paths.append(path)
                break
    newest = 0.0
    for path in paths:
        try:
            newest = max(newest, os.stat(path).st_mtime)
        except OSError:
            pass
    return newest or None


def mtime(path):
    try:
        return os.stat(path).st_mtime
    except OSError:
        return 0.0


def interactive_in(cwd):
    """Pids of every interactive `claude` (no -p/--print) whose cwd is that directory."""
    out = []
    for pid in os.listdir("/proc"):
        if not pid.isdigit():
            continue
        try:
            if open(f"/proc/{pid}/comm").read().strip() != "claude":
                continue
            argv = open(f"/proc/{pid}/cmdline", "rb").read().decode("utf-8", "replace").split("\0")
            if any(a in ("-p", "--print") for a in argv):
                continue
            if os.path.realpath(os.readlink(f"/proc/{pid}/cwd")) == cwd:
                out.append(pid)
        except OSError:
            continue
    return out


# ── reality ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def procs():
    """One pass over /proc → (live tracks, {ppids}, {pids holding an interactive session}, {track: [worker pids]},
    {track: [loop pids]}). A worker is a headless claude (the budget flag is on its command line)."""
    live, ppids, root = set(), set(), WTS + os.sep
    workers, loops, parent, inter, sessions = {}, {}, {}, set(), set()
    for pid in os.listdir("/proc"):
        if not pid.isdigit():
            continue
        try:
            with open(f"/proc/{pid}/status") as f:
                for ln in f:
                    if ln.startswith("PPid:"):
                        ppids.add(ln.split()[1])
                        parent[pid] = ln.split()[1]
                        break
            argv = open(f"/proc/{pid}/cmdline", "rb").read().decode("utf-8", "replace").split("\0")
            comm = open(f"/proc/{pid}/comm").read().strip()
        except OSError:
            continue
        for i, a in enumerate(argv):
            if a and os.path.basename(a) == "cc-loop" and len(argv) > i + 2 and argv[i + 1] and argv[i + 2]:
                live.add(f"{argv[i + 1]}/{argv[i + 2]}")
                loops.setdefault(f"{argv[i + 1]}/{argv[i + 2]}", []).append(int(pid))
                break
        if comm == "claude":
            if not any(a in ("-p", "--print") for a in argv):
                inter.add(pid)
            try:
                cwd = os.readlink(f"/proc/{pid}/cwd")
            except OSError:
                continue
            if cwd.startswith(root):
                key = "/".join(cwd[len(root):].split(os.sep)[:2])
                live.add(key)
                if any(a.startswith("--max-budget-usd") for a in argv):
                    workers.setdefault(key, []).append(int(pid))
    for pid in inter:                                   # everything above an interactive session holds it
        up, seen = pid, set()
        while up and up not in seen and up != "1":
            seen.add(up)
            sessions.add(up)
            up = parent.get(up, "")
    return live, ppids, sessions, workers, loops


def idle_for(repo, track, wt):
    """Seconds since the track last moved: journal, loop log, runs, or the worktree's HEAD."""
    newest = 0.0
    st = f"{STATE}/{repo}/{track}"
    for path in (f"{st}/progress.md", f"{st}/loop.log", f"{st}/runs", f"{wt}/.git"):
        try:
            newest = max(newest, os.stat(path).st_mtime)
        except OSError:
            pass
    try:
        gd = open(f"{wt}/.git").read().strip()
        if gd.startswith("gitdir:"):
            newest = max(newest, os.stat(os.path.join(gd[7:].strip(), "HEAD")).st_mtime)
    except OSError:
        pass
    return max(0.0, now() - newest) if newest else 0.0


def limit_stamp():
    """cc-limit's stamp as (until, observers): "<until>\\t<how>\\t<first-seen>\\t<model>\\t<observers>"."""
    try:
        f = open(os.environ.get("CC_LIMIT_STAMP") or f"{STATE}/claude-limit").read().split("\n")[0].split("\t")
        obs = [k for k in (f[4].split(",") if len(f) > 4 else [])
               if len(k) == 8 and all(c in "0123456789abcdef" for c in k)]
        return float(f[0]), len(obs)
    except Exception:
        return 0.0, 0


def limit_active():
    """A usage limit standing over the box: two runs hit it. One run's limit binds that run alone."""
    until, n = limit_stamp()
    return until > now() and n >= 2


def limit_started():
    """When the last usage-limit episode cc-limit resumed from began (epoch), or 0: "<started>\\t<reset>\\t<resumed>"."""
    try:
        f = open(os.environ.get("CC_LIMIT_RESUMED") or f"{STATE}/limit-resumed").read().split("\n")[0].split("\t")
        if len(f) != 3:
            return 0.0
        at, until = float(f[0]), float(f[1])
        return at if 0 < at and 0 < until <= now() else 0.0
    except Exception:
        return 0.0


def limit_until():
    until, n = limit_stamp()
    return until if until > now() and n >= 2 else 0.0


def runaway(f, seen_before, wedged=WEDGED):
    """Pure: why this live track is spending without working, or ""."""
    if f.get("orphans"):
        return ("a headless worker with no cc-loop above it — nothing will time it out, reap it or commit "
                f"what it writes ({len(f['orphans'])} process(es), {f['idle'] / 3600:.1f} h since anything moved)")
    if f.get("workers") and not f.get("limited") and f["idle"] >= wedged and seen_before:
        return (f"its loop is wedged: alive with nothing moved for {f['idle'] / 3600:.1f} h — no commit, no "
                "journal line, no iteration, and no usage limit to be waiting on")
    return ""


def waits_for(f):
    """Pure: ("person"|"clock"|"", why). Only the worker's own STATUS: BLOCKED line names a person."""
    jk, jt = f.get("journal") or (None, "")
    if jk == "BLOCKED":
        return ("person", jt or "it stood down without saying what it needs")
    if f.get("limited") and f.get("loops") and not f.get("workers"):
        return ("clock", "a Claude usage limit — the loop resumes by itself, nobody is being asked")
    return ("", "")


def panes(lines, ppids, sessions=(), t0=None):
    """Pure reading of a `tmux list-panes` listing: (tracks whose window has something running, {track: seconds
    since the window moved}, {"<window id>:<server pid>": window name} for windows an interactive session is in)."""
    live, idle, wins, t0 = set(), {}, {}, t0 if t0 is not None else now()
    for ln in lines:
        f = ln.split("\t")
        if len(f) < 2 or f[1].strip() not in ppids:
            continue                                    # nothing running in that pane: a leftover window
        if len(f) > 3 and f[3].strip() and f[1].strip() in sessions:
            wins[f[3].strip()] = f[0]
        if f[0].count("/") != 1:
            continue                                    # a track window is `<repo>/<track>`
        live.add(f[0])
        try:
            act = float(f[2]) if len(f) > 2 and f[2].strip() else 0.0
        except ValueError:
            act = 0.0
        if act:
            was = max(0.0, t0 - act)
            idle[f[0]] = min(idle[f[0]], was) if f[0] in idle else was
    return live, idle, wins


def tmux_live(ppids, sessions=()):
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["tmux", "list-panes", "-a", "-F",
                              "#{window_name}\t#{pane_pid}\t#{window_activity}\t#{window_id}:#{pid}"],
                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
    except Exception:
        return set(), {}, {}
    return panes(out.stdout.splitlines(), ppids, sessions)


def journal(repo, track):
    """(kind, text) from the last STATUS line the worker left."""
    try:
        body = open(f"{STATE}/{repo}/{track}/progress.md", errors="replace").read().splitlines()[-400:]
    except OSError:
        return (None, "")
    for ln in reversed(body):
        s = ln.strip()
        if s.upper().startswith("STATUS: DONE"):
            return ("DONE", "")
        if s.upper().startswith("STATUS: BLOCKED"):
            return ("BLOCKED", s[len("STATUS: BLOCKED"):].lstrip(": ").strip())
    return (None, "")


def loop_end(repo, track):
    """cc-loop's last word, only if it came after the last iteration it started."""
    try:
        body = open(f"{STATE}/{repo}/{track}/loop.log", errors="replace").read().splitlines()[-200:]
    except OSError:
        return ""
    for ln in reversed(body):
        m = re.search(r"\bexit (\d+): (.+)", ln)
        if m:
            return f"exit {m.group(1)}: {m.group(2)}"[:160]
        if re.search(r"\biter \d+/\d+ start", ln):
            return ""
    return ""


def pr_state(repo, url, net=True):
    """MERGED / OPEN / CLOSED, '?' when GitHub could not answer, None when never asked."""
    if not net or not url or not shutil.which("gh"):
        return None if not net else "?"
    cwd = f"{DEV}/{repo}"
    p = sh("gh", "pr", "view", str(url), "--json", "state", "-q", ".state",
           cwd=cwd if os.path.isdir(cwd) else None, timeout=20)
    s = (p.stdout if p is not None else "").strip().upper()
    return s if s in ("MERGED", "OPEN", "CLOSED") else "?"


def branch_prs(repo, branch, net=True):
    """[(number, STATE, merged_at, created_at)] for the PRs opened from <branch>, newest first; `created_at` is what
    false_nags() holds a nag against. None when GitHub could not be asked."""
    cwd = f"{DEV}/{repo}"
    if not net or not branch or not shutil.which("gh") or not os.path.isdir(cwd):
        return None
    p = sh("gh", "pr", "list", "--head", branch, "--state", "all", "--limit", "10",
           "--json", "number,state,mergedAt,createdAt", cwd=cwd, timeout=20)
    if p is None or p.returncode:
        return None
    try:
        return [(int(r["number"]), str(r.get("state") or "").upper(), epoch(r.get("mergedAt")), epoch(r.get("createdAt")))
                for r in json.loads(p.stdout or "[]")]
    except Exception:
        return None


REVIEW_MARK = "cc-land-review"      # the HTML comment the lander writes a review down in
VERDICT_RE = (re.compile(rf"\A\s*<!-- {re.escape(REVIEW_MARK)} v2 change=[0-9a-f]+[^>]*? head=([0-9a-f]+)"
                         r"[^>]*? verdict=(LAND-AFTER-FIX|DO-NOT-LAND|LAND)\b"),
              re.compile(rf"\A\s*<!-- {re.escape(REVIEW_MARK)} ([0-9a-f]{{12}}) "
                         r"(LAND-AFTER-FIX|DO-NOT-LAND|LAND) -->"))
STOPPING = ("DO-NOT-LAND", "LAND-AFTER-FIX")


def refused(repo, url, net=True):
    """The stopping verdict recorded on the PR's current head, or "". The last marker about that head stands;
    a verdict about a head the PR moved past is spent. Anchored at the comment's start: a finding quoting a marker
    is not a verdict."""
    if not net or not url or not shutil.which("gh"):
        return ""
    cwd = f"{DEV}/{repo}"
    p = sh("gh", "pr", "view", str(url), "--json", "headRefOid,comments", cwd=cwd if os.path.isdir(cwd) else None, timeout=20)
    if p is None or p.returncode:
        return ""
    try:
        j = json.loads(p.stdout or "{}")
        head = str(j.get("headRefOid") or "")
        out = ""
        for c in j.get("comments") or []:
            m = next((x for x in (r.match(str(c.get("body") or "")) for r in VERDICT_RE) if x), None)
            if m and head and head.startswith(m.group(1)):
                out = m.group(2)
        return out if out in STOPPING else ""
    except Exception:
        return ""


def alert(msg):
    """#alerts, best-effort; under CC_NOTIFY_LOG_ONLY (every suite sets it) it goes to the log."""
    if os.environ.get("CC_NOTIFY_LOG_ONLY"):
        try:
            with open(os.environ.get("CC_NOTIFY_LOG") or f"{STATE}/notify.log", "a") as fh:
                fh.write(f"alerts\t{msg}\n")
        except OSError:
            pass
        return
    sh(f"{BIN}/cc-slack", "post", "-c", "#alerts", msg, timeout=30)


def host_marker(repo, track, name, home=None):
    """Where the host's <name> marker for this track is: ~/.cc/push-state for a member workspace (the worktree's
    copy there is the member's own), else <wt>/.cc/<name>. Every reader follows this one rule."""
    h = home or HOME
    if os.path.exists(f"{h}/dev/{repo}/.cc/member-workspace"):
        return f"{h}/.cc/push-state/{repo}/{track}/{name}"
    return f"{h}/.cc/worktrees/{repo}/{track}/.cc/{name}"


def push_marker(repo, track, home=None):
    return host_marker(repo, track, "push.err", home)


def commit_marker(repo, track, home=None):
    """The refused-checkpoint marker: the host's, or the member's own in-boundary one; whichever exists, the host's first."""
    h = home or HOME
    host = host_marker(repo, track, "checkpoint.err", h)
    member = f"{h}/.cc/worktrees/{repo}/{track}/.cc/checkpoint.err"
    return next((p for p in (host, member) if os.path.exists(p)), host)


def wt_branch(wt):
    """The branch checked out in <wt>, or "" (detached, no checkout of its own, git would not answer)."""
    if not os.path.exists(f"{wt}/.git"):
        return ""
    r = sh("git", "-C", wt, "symbolic-ref", "--short", "HEAD", timeout=10)
    return "" if r is None or r.returncode else r.stdout.strip()


def branch_unpushed(wt):
    """Does this worktree hold commits origin lacks? True / False / None (cannot tell: no branch, never on origin).
    The push.err marker is not this answer: nothing clears it when the branch reaches origin another way."""
    br = wt_branch(wt)
    if not br:
        return None
    up = sh("git", "-C", wt, "rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"refs/remotes/origin/{br}", timeout=10)
    if up is None or up.returncode:
        return None
    anc = sh("git", "-C", wt, "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", "HEAD", up.stdout.strip(), timeout=10)
    return None if anc is None else anc.returncode != 0


def has_remote(repo):
    p = sh("git", "-C", f"{DEV}/{repo}", "remote", "get-url", "origin", timeout=10)
    return p is not None and p.returncode == 0


# ── the decision ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def idle_session(f, idle=IDLE):
    """Pure: live only because a session sits open at its prompt, and has for `idle`. A worker or a loop is work."""
    return bool(f.get("live")) and not f.get("workers") and not f.get("loops") and f.get("pane_idle", 0.0) >= idle


def decide(f):
    """Pure: facts in, [(kind, status|None, why)] out. fix = decidable, applied silently · ask = needs a person,
    applied when it also has one right status · info = could not tell · held = known and nobody's · stop = ended."""
    st, pr, has_pr = f["status"], f.get("pr_state") or "", bool(f.get("pr"))
    live = f["live"] or bool(f.get("agent_live"))       # a live session's `agent` mark counts as alive
    jk = (f.get("journal") or (None, ""))[0]
    who, wwhy = waits_for(f)
    if (f.get("kind") or "track") == "session":         # a channel, not a task: only its question is drift
        if who == "person" and st not in TERMINAL:
            return [("ask", "waiting", "it is waiting on you: " + wwhy)]
        if st == "waiting":
            return [("fix", "running" if f["live"] else "queued", "its question was answered")]
        return []
    out, settled = [], False
    # NEVER RAN: no cc-task claim, not started by `cc <repo> <track>` or cc-handoff, no journal or loop log, and no
    # worktree — a row made with its project channel and left, or a word set by hand. "Killed, or the box restarted"
    # and "its worktree is gone" say something was lost; nothing was (raised 2026-09-11, a member workspace's
    # row). The brief: "a row that has never run is reported as never started, not as lost".
    never_ran = not (f.get("delivery") or f.get("started") or f.get("worked")) and not f["wt_exists"]
    if f.get("stop_why"):
        out.append(("stop", "blocked", f["stop_why"]))
        settled = True
    elif who == "person" and st not in TERMINAL:        # a declaration outranks presence, and is said every run
        out.append(("ask", "waiting", "it is waiting on you: " + wwhy))
        settled = True
    elif who == "clock" and st not in TERMINAL + QUEUED:
        out.append(("held", None, "waiting on the clock, not on you: " + wwhy))
        settled = True
    elif st in QUEUED + ("blocked", "waiting") and (live if st in QUEUED
                                                    else (f["live"] and not idle_session(f))):
        # `blocked`/`waiting` is a word a session set; a session sitting at its prompt in the worktree is not
        # work in flight, and flipping the word back on its presence alone reverted a correction within minutes
        # (a member workspace's row, three times over two pulses, raised 2026-09-10). The brief: "a status a
        # session set is not reverted by decide() while no pane is live" — only a worker, a loop or a pane moved
        # inside IDLE overrides it. A bare `agent` mark does not: the re-mark loop keeps it fresh for as long as
        # the seat lives, so it flipped such a row back every pass with no pane in the window at all (raised
        # 2026-09-19). The mark still flips QUEUED, which is nobody's word, and still keeps the row off the
        # abandoned path below — it is the only thing on the box saying somebody is on it.
        out.append(("fix", "running", "a worker is in its worktree" if f["live"]
                    else "a live session is doing it in a subagent"))
        settled = True
    elif not live and st in ("running", "waiting") and f["age"] >= f.get("grace", GRACE):
        settled = True
        if jk == "DONE" and pr == "MERGED":
            out.append(("fix", "merged", "it finished and its PR merged"))
        elif st == "waiting" and (jk == "DONE" or pr == "OPEN"):   # `waiting` is a person's word: only a merge moves it
            if not has_pr:
                out.append(("ask", None, "it finished but no PR was ever opened"))
            elif pr == "CLOSED":
                out.append(("ask", None, "its PR was closed without merging"))
        elif jk == "DONE" and has_pr:
            out.append(("fix", "review", "it finished and its PR is open"))
        elif jk == "DONE":
            out.append(("ask", "review", "it finished but no PR was ever opened"))
        elif f.get("loop_end"):
            out.append(("ask", "blocked", "its loop stopped — " + f["loop_end"]))
        elif pr == "MERGED":
            out.append(("fix", "merged", "its PR merged"))
        elif pr == "OPEN":
            out.append(("fix", "review", "its PR is open"))
        else:                                           # a cold mark says what happened; then never-ran; then lost
            out.append(("ask", "blocked", f.get("agent_stale")
                        or ("never started: no claim, no worktree, no journal — the word was set by hand, "
                            "nothing was lost" if never_ran
                            else "no worker, and nothing says why (killed, or the box restarted)")))
    if not settled:                                     # the PR outranks any status but a live process
        if pr == "MERGED" and st != "merged":
            out.append(("fix", "merged", "its PR merged"))
        elif pr == "OPEN" and st in TERMINAL:
            out.append(("fix", "review", "its PR is still open"))
        elif pr == "CLOSED" and st not in TERMINAL:
            out.append(("ask", None, "its PR was closed without merging"))
        elif pr == "?":
            out.append(("info", None, "could not read its PR state"))
    if st == "review" and not has_pr and f.get("has_remote"):
        out.append(("ask", None, "it is waiting on a PR that was never opened"))
    word = next((s for _, s, _ in out if s), "") or st   # the word this run landed on
    finished = word in TERMINAL                          # the work landed: a gone worktree or branch is success
    landed_elsewhere = st == "review" and has_pr and pr in ("OPEN", "MERGED")   # a PR from a worktree of its own
    # a row nothing ever dispatched (no claim, never started, no journal) is supposed to have no worktree
    if (not f["wt_exists"] and not finished and word not in QUEUED
            and (f.get("delivery") or f.get("started") or f.get("worked"))
            and not f.get("agent") and not landed_elsewhere):
        out.append(("ask", None, "its worktree is gone"))
    safety = []                                          # work about to be lost: the host's, never muted by a hold
    if f.get("commit_err") and not finished:
        safety.append(("ask", None, "its last checkpoint would not commit — that work is only in the worktree"))
    if f.get("push_err") and (f.get("unpushed") is True or (f.get("unpushed") is None and not finished)):
        safety.append(("ask", None, "its branch is not pushed"))   # True is told on a finished row too: sweep rule 1 would delete it
    out += safety
    hold = str(f.get("held") or "").strip()              # a person stopped this: the guesses go quiet, the rest stands
    if hold:
        out = [r for r in out if r[0] in ("fix", "stop") or r in safety
               or (r[0], r[1]) == ("ask", "waiting")] + [("held", None, "held: " + hold)]
    return out


def effective(f, recs):
    """Pure: the one word for a track. What decide() would set outranks the board; `idle` narrows `running`."""
    session = (f.get("kind") or "track") == "session"
    word = next((st for _, st, _ in recs if st), "") or (f["status"] or "queued")
    if session:
        return "session" if word != "waiting" else word
    if word == "todo":
        return "queued"
    return "idle" if word == "running" and idle_session(f) else word


def pending(f, state):
    """Pure: finished, PR open, nobody landed it. A board that says `waiting` is a person's word and never pending."""
    return state == "review" and (f.get("pr_state") or "") == "OPEN" and f["status"] != "waiting"


LAND_ARGV = re.compile(r"(?:^|[\s/])cc-land\s+(?:queue\s+)?([A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9._-]*)"
                       r"((?:\s+(?:--no-review|--re-review|[0-9]+))+)(?=\s|$)")


def pr_number(url):
    m = re.search(r"([0-9]+)/?\s*$", str(url or ""))
    return int(m.group(1)) if m else None


def landing():
    """{(repo, pr)} somebody is landing: a job under ~/.cc/state/land/, a work record under land/root/ touched
    inside BETWEEN_ROUNDS, or a live lander argv naming the PR (a session's prompt quoting it does not count)."""
    out = set()
    for path in glob.glob(f"{STATE}/land/*.json") + glob.glob(f"{STATE}/land/root/*.json"):
        try:
            if "/root/" in path and now() - os.path.getmtime(path) > BETWEEN_ROUNDS:
                continue
            j = json.load(open(path))
            if j.get("repo") and j.get("pr"):
                out.add((j["repo"], int(j["pr"])))
        except Exception:
            continue
    me = os.getpid()
    for d in os.listdir("/proc"):
        if not d.isdigit() or int(d) == me:
            continue
        try:
            argv = open(f"/proc/{d}/cmdline", "rb").read().decode(errors="replace").split("\0")
        except OSError:
            continue
        if any(os.path.basename(a) == "claude" for a in argv):
            continue
        for m in LAND_ARGV.finditer(" ".join(argv)):
            out.update((m.group(1), int(n)) for n in re.findall(r"[0-9]+", m.group(2)))
    return out


ORPHAN_WHY = "a worktree with no board entry"   # orphans()'s one finding, and the one ask false_nags() can re-read
FALSE_NAG = "notification/false-action-needed"   # the catalogue kind: "a wake or a nag names something a person or a seat must do"


def land_windows(repo, pr):
    """[(start, end)] epochs during which cc-land had <repo>#<pr> in hand, from its queue log — `queued` opens a
    window, the next `done` closes it, one still open runs to now. The log is kept after the job file and the work
    record are gone (cc-land: queue.log is KEPT after the job file is drained), which is why it is the source here
    and not landing(): by the pass that finds a nag cleared, the landing that cleared it has taken its files."""
    out, start, tag = [], None, f" {repo}#{pr} "
    try:
        for ln in open(f"{HOME}/.cc/state/land/queue.log"):
            if tag not in ln + " ":
                continue
            ts, _, ev = ln.rstrip("\n").partition("\t")
            word = ev.split(" ", 1)[0]
            if word == "queued" and start is None:
                start = epoch(ts)
            elif word == "done" and start is not None:
                out.append((start, epoch(ts))); start = None
    except OSError:
        return out
    if start is not None:
        out.append((start, now()))
    return out


def pr_times(repo, url, net=True):
    """(created_at, merged_at) epochs for a PR a board row names, 0.0 where GitHub says none; None when it could not
    be asked — no evidence, and false_nags() writes nothing on no evidence."""
    if not net or not url or not shutil.which("gh"):
        return None
    cwd = f"{DEV}/{repo}"
    p = sh("gh", "pr", "view", str(url), "--json", "createdAt,mergedAt", cwd=cwd if os.path.isdir(cwd) else None, timeout=20)
    if p is None or p.returncode:
        return None
    try:
        j = json.loads(p.stdout or "{}")
        return epoch(j.get("createdAt")), epoch(j.get("mergedAt"))
    except Exception:
        return None


def record_failure(scope, kind, observed, ts, evidence=(), links=(), cost=("contexts=1",)):
    """One line to the failure ledger, through cc-failures, and nothing else: no exception leaves here, no exit code
    is read, and the pass that called it decides exactly what it would have decided without it."""
    argv = [sib("cc-failures"), "record", "--scope", scope, "--kind", kind, "--observed", observed,
            "--writer", "cc-reconcile", "--detector", "box",
            "--detector-evidence", "the authoritative state, read on the pass that found the nag cleared, carries a time before the nag",
            "--expected", "a wake or a nag names something a person or a seat must do",
            "--ts", time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(ts))]
    for e in evidence:
        argv += ["--evidence", e]
    for l in links:
        argv += ["--link", l]
    for c in cost:
        argv += ["--cost", c]
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
        how = "recorded " + r.stdout.strip() if r.returncode == 0 else f"writer failed rc={r.returncode}: {r.stderr.strip()[:160]}"
    except Exception as e:
        how = f"writer failed: {e.__class__.__name__}"
    try:
        os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
        with open(f"{STATE}/reconcile.log", "a") as log:
            log.write(f"{time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime())}\tfailure\t{scope} {kind}\t{how}\n")
    except OSError:
        pass


def false_nags(gone, prs, net=True):
    """A nag that went away is read once more against the authoritative state AT THE TIME IT WENT OUT, and one that
    the state disproves is written to the failure ledger (docs/design-failure-noticing-2026-09-11.md, The writers:
    "cc-reconcile (a nag the authoritative state disproved)"). `gone` is {memo: when} for the memos the seen-ledger
    just dropped, `prs` {repo/track: pr} off the board. Two shapes are decidable by a time the box did not consult
    when it nagged, and only those are written:
      · `offered <repo>/<track> <pr>` and `alerted <repo>/<track>` — "review and land it", to the session or the
        owner. Disproved when a landing already had the PR: cc-land's queue log shows a `queued`..`done` window
        around the nag (land_windows), its work record's `first` predates the nag, or the PR had merged before it.
      · `<repo>/<track>: a worktree with no board entry` — disproved when a PR from that branch was already open at
        the nag: created before it and not merged more than BETWEEN_ROUNDS before it, the same forgiveness orphans()
        itself gives, or a landing window around it.
    Everything else that cleared — a gone worktree restored, a branch pushed, a PR closed and settled — is a person's
    doing or undecidable here, and nothing is written; nor is anything written on NO evidence (GitHub unreadable).
    One record per nag, at the nag's own time, and the ledger's own episode rule folds the session's line and the
    owner's page about one PR into one. Never raises; never changes the pass."""
    def when(t):
        return time.strftime("%H:%MZ", time.gmtime(t))
    seen = set()
    for memo, at in sorted(gone.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]):
        try:
            at = float(at or 0)
            if not at:
                continue
            m = re.match(r"^(offered|alerted) ([^/ ]+)/([^ ]+)(?: (.+))?$", memo)
            if m:
                word, repo, track, url = m.groups()
                url = url or prs.get(f"{repo}/{track}") or ""
                n = pr_number(url)
                if not n or (repo, n) in seen:
                    continue
                why = ""
                if any(a <= at <= b for a, b in land_windows(repo, n)):
                    why = "cc-land's queue log shows a landing of it in flight across that minute"
                else:
                    try:
                        first = epoch(json.load(open(f"{HOME}/.cc/state/land/root/{repo}-{n}.json")).get("first"))
                    except Exception:
                        first = 0.0
                    if first and first <= at:
                        why = f"cc-land's work record says it had the PR since {when(first)}"
                    else:
                        t = pr_times(repo, url, net)
                        if t and t[1] and t[1] <= at:
                            why = f"the PR had merged at {when(t[1])}"
                if not why:
                    continue
                seen.add((repo, n))
                to = "the repo's session" if word == "offered" else "the owner"
                record_failure(repo, FALSE_NAG,
                               f"the board watchdog told {to} to review and land PR #{n} ({repo}/{track}) at {when(at)}, and {why}: nothing was needed",
                               at, evidence=[f"memo={memo}", why], links=[f"row={repo}/{track}", f"pr={n}", f"source=cc-reconcile:{memo}@{int(at)}"],
                               cost=["contexts=1"] if word == "offered" else ["owner-time=1 page"])
                continue
            m = re.match(r"^([^/ ]+)/([^:]+): " + re.escape(ORPHAN_WHY) + "$", memo)
            if not m:
                continue
            repo, track = m.groups()
            wt = f"{WTS}/{repo}/{track}"
            cands = [b for b in ([wt_branch(wt)] if os.path.isdir(wt) else [track, f"track/{track}"]) if b]
            hit = None
            for b in cands:
                for n, st, merged, created in (branch_prs(repo, b, net) or []):
                    if created and created <= at and (not merged or merged >= at - BETWEEN_ROUNDS):
                        hit = (n, st, "was already open" if not merged or merged > at else f"had merged {(at - merged) / 60:.0f} min before")
                    elif any(a <= at <= b_ for a, b_ in land_windows(repo, n)):
                        hit = (n, st, "was being landed")
                    if hit:
                        break
                if hit:
                    break
            if not hit or (repo, hit[0]) in seen:
                continue
            seen.add((repo, hit[0]))
            record_failure(repo, FALSE_NAG,
                           f"the board watchdog reported {repo}/{track} as a worktree with no board entry at {when(at)}, and its PR #{hit[0]} {hit[2]}: a delivery in flight, not a leftover",
                           at, evidence=[f"memo={memo}", f"pr #{hit[0]} {hit[1]} {hit[2]}"],
                           links=[f"row={repo}/{track}", f"pr={hit[0]}", f"source=cc-reconcile:{memo}@{int(at)}"])
        except Exception:
            continue


def snapshot(rows, limit=0.0):
    """The dict written to ~/.cc/state/reconcile.json: per track the word, presence, who it waits on and why."""
    return {"at": stamp(), "epoch": int(now()), "limit_until": int(limit or 0),
            "tracks": {f"{repo}/{track}": {"state": state, "board": f["status"],
                                           "kind": f.get("kind") or "track",
                                           "live": bool(f["live"] or f.get("agent_live")),
                                           "waiting_on": who, "why": why,
                                           "idle_for": int(f.get("pane_idle") or 0),
                                           "loop": bool(f.get("loops")), "agent": bool(f.get("agent_live")),
                                           "held": str(f.get("held") or "").strip()}
                       for repo, track, f, state, who, why in rows}}


# ── the run ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def paused(target):
    """`cc-pause is <target>`: parked. A cc-pause that cannot answer is "not paused"."""
    p = sh(sib("cc-pause"), "is", str(target), timeout=10)
    return p is not None and p.returncode == 0


def ccboard():
    """cc-board imported as a module beside THIS copy: its opener `read` and the fixture rule (`reals`, `real`, FIXTURE)."""
    if not hasattr(ccboard, "mod"):
        import importlib.machinery, importlib.util
        s = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("ccboard", importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(
            "ccboard", os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "cc-board")))
        ccboard.mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(s); s.loader.exec_module(ccboard.mod)
    return ccboard.mod


def board_read(path):
    """A board file through cc-board's opener (a planted pipe is refused, not a hang). None = no board there."""
    return ccboard().read(path)


def row_title(repo, track):
    """What a person calls a row: its board title, else its name in words. A hyphenated name means nothing to him."""
    try:
        ti = str((board_read(f"{BOARDS}/{repo}.json").get("tracks") or {}).get(track, {}).get("title") or "")
    except Exception:
        ti = ""
    return ti or re.sub(r"[-_]", " ", track)


def spoken_hours(sec):
    """A span as you would say it aloud: "an hour", "12 hours", "3 days"."""
    h = max(1, round(sec / 3600))
    return "an hour" if h == 1 else f"{h} hours" if h < 48 else f"{round(h / 24)} days"


def boards():
    """Every real board, sorted: (path, board or None if unreadable). A `_cc<suite><pid>` board is a board only to
    a process under <pid> (cc-board `reals`)."""
    out = []
    for n in ccboard().reals(sorted(os.path.basename(fn) for fn in glob.glob(f"{BOARDS}/*.json"))):
        fn = f"{BOARDS}/{n}"
        try:
            out.append((fn, board_read(fn)))
        except Exception:
            out.append((fn, None))
    return out


def facts(repos, net=True, grace=GRACE, no_stop=False, wedged=WEDGED, mark=AGENT_MARK):
    """Every board track with what the box says about it. Yields (repo, track, board_track, facts)."""
    live, ppids, sessions, workers, loops = procs()
    tlive, pane_idle, wins = tmux_live(ppids, sessions)
    live |= tlive
    seen, limited = ledger(f"{STATE}/wedged.json"), limit_active()
    started = limit_started()
    prs, remotes, t0, wp = 0, {}, now(), None
    for fn, d in boards():
        if d is None:
            continue
        repo = d.get("repo") or os.path.basename(fn)[:-5]
        if repos and repo not in repos:
            continue
        for track, t in sorted(d.get("tracks", {}).items()):
            st, pr = t.get("status", ""), t.get("pr", "")
            want_pr = bool(pr) and st != "merged"       # `merged` is derived from the PR: re-reading it buys nothing
            ask_pr = want_pr and prs < PRMAX
            prs += bool(ask_pr)
            wt = t.get("worktree") or f"{WTS}/{repo}/{track}"
            if repo not in remotes:
                remotes[repo] = has_remote(repo)
            key = f"{repo}/{track}"
            ag = (t.get("agent") or "").strip()
            if ag and wp is None:                       # one tmux read per run, and none on a board with no marks
                wp = window_panes()
            ag_live, ag_stale = mark_why(t, wins, repo, t0, mark, started,
                                         seat_turn(wp.get(ag)) if ag and wp else None)
            f = {"agent": (t.get("agent") or "").strip(), "agent_live": ag_live, "agent_stale": ag_stale,
                 "held": str(t.get("held") or "").strip(),
                 "repo": repo, "track": track, "status": st, "pr": pr, "kind": t.get("kind") or "track",
                 "pr_state": pr_state(repo, pr, net) if ask_pr else ("?" if want_pr and net else None),
                 "live": key in live, "wt_exists": os.path.isdir(wt),
                 "delivery": os.path.exists(f"{STATE}/{repo}/{track}/delivery.json"),   # cc-task's claim record
                 "started": bool(t.get("started")),                                      # `cc <repo> <track>` / cc-handoff
                 "worked": os.path.exists(f"{STATE}/{repo}/{track}/progress.md")
                           or os.path.exists(f"{STATE}/{repo}/{track}/loop.log"),        # the legacy worker path's trace
                 "age": max(0.0, t0 - epoch(t.get("updated") or t.get("created"))), "grace": grace,
                 "journal": journal(repo, track), "loop_end": loop_end(repo, track),
                 "commit_err": os.path.exists(commit_marker(repo, track)),
                 "push_err": os.path.exists(push_marker(repo, track)), "has_remote": remotes[repo],
                 "unpushed": branch_unpushed(wt) if os.path.exists(push_marker(repo, track)) else False,
                 "workers": workers.get(key, []), "loops": loops.get(key, []), "limited": limited,
                 "orphans": workers.get(key, []) if not loops.get(key) else [],
                 "idle": idle_for(repo, track, wt) if workers.get(key) else 0.0,
                 "pane_idle": pane_idle.get(key, 0.0)}
            f["stop_why"] = "" if no_stop else runaway(f, t0 - float(seen.get(key) or 0) <= WEDGE_SEEN, wedged)
            f["wedged_now"] = bool(f["workers"] and not f["limited"] and f["idle"] >= wedged)
            yield repo, track, t, f


def orphans(repos, net=True, grace=GRACE, busy=None):
    """Worktrees with no board entry: reported only. Skipped when a row names the directory, it is younger than
    `grace`, its branch has an OPEN PR, its PR is being landed, or its PR MERGED inside BETWEEN_ROUNDS."""
    known, claimed = set(), set()
    for fn, d in boards():
        if d is None:
            return []
        repo = d.get("repo") or os.path.basename(fn)[:-5]
        for t, tr in (d.get("tracks") or {}).items():
            known.add(f"{repo}/{t}")
            if (tr or {}).get("worktree"):
                claimed.add(os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser(tr["worktree"])))
    out, asked, t0 = [], 0, now()
    for p in sorted(glob.glob(f"{WTS}/*/*")):
        repo, track = p.split(os.sep)[-2:]
        if not ccboard().real(repo) or not os.path.isdir(p) or f"{repo}/{track}" in known or (repos and repo not in repos):
            continue
        if os.path.realpath(p) in claimed:
            continue
        try:
            if now() - os.path.getmtime(p) < grace:
                continue
        except OSError:
            pass
        prs = None
        if asked < ORPHANPRS:
            asked += 1
            prs = branch_prs(repo, wt_branch(p), net)
        if prs:
            busy = landing() if busy is None else busy
            if any(st == "OPEN" or (repo, n) in busy or (st == "MERGED" and t0 - at <= BETWEEN_ROUNDS)
                   for n, st, at, _ in prs):
                continue
        out.append((repo, track, ("ask", None, "a worktree with no board entry")))
    return out


def end_it(pids):
    """SIGTERM to each process's whole group, never our own; one already gone counts as ended."""
    mine, ok = os.getpgid(0), False
    for pid in pids:
        try:
            pg = os.getpgid(pid)
        except OSError:
            ok = True
            continue
        try:
            if pg != mine:
                os.killpg(pg, signal.SIGTERM)
            else:
                os.kill(pid, signal.SIGTERM)
            ok = True
        except OSError:
            pass
    return ok


def board(*args):
    p = sh(f"{BIN}/cc-board", *args, timeout=30)
    return p is not None and p.returncode == 0


def ledger(path, write=None):
    """{finding: when}: read, or written atomically."""
    if write is None:
        try:
            return json.load(open(path))
        except Exception:
            return {}
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
    tmp = path + ".tmp"
    json.dump(write, open(tmp, "w"))
    os.replace(tmp, path)
    return write


def snap_file():
    """The snapshot file's tracks while it is fresh, else {} — the fallback every reader shares."""
    try:
        snap = json.load(open(f"{STATE}/reconcile.json"))
        ep = snap.get("epoch") if isinstance(snap, dict) else None
        if not isinstance(ep, int) or ep <= 0 or now() - ep >= FRESH:
            return {}
        t = snap.get("tracks")
        return {k: v for k, v in t.items() if isinstance(v, dict)} if isinstance(t, dict) else {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def view():
    """The snapshot as TSV: repo/track · state · waiting_on · why, escaped as jq's @tsv would. Stale: no rows."""
    def cell(v):
        s = "" if v is None or v is False else str(v)
        return s.replace("\\", "\\\\").replace("\t", "\\t").replace("\n", "\\n").replace("\r", "\\r")
    rows = ["\t".join(cell(x) for x in (k, t.get("state"), t.get("waiting_on"), t.get("why")))
            for k, t in snap_file().items()]
    sys.stdout.buffer.write("".join(r + "\n" for r in rows).encode("utf-8"))
    return 0


# ── the sweep ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def dur(s):
    for unit, div in (("d", 86400), ("h", 3600), ("m", 60)):
        if s >= div:
            return f"{int(s // div)}{unit}"
    return f"{int(s)}s"


def dirty(wt):
    """Uncommitted work (untracked included). No `.git` there: nothing to lose. git refusing to answer: dirty."""
    if not os.path.exists(f"{wt}/.git"):
        return False
    p = sh("git", "-C", wt, "status", "--porcelain", timeout=60)
    return p is None or p.returncode != 0 or bool(p.stdout.strip())


def terminal_since(d, track, t):
    """When the track's status last became merged/done (the board log; `updated` is bumped by notes too)."""
    for e in reversed(d.get("log") or []):
        if e.get("track") == track and str(e.get("msg", "")).startswith("status -> "):
            return epoch(e.get("ts")) if e["msg"][len("status -> "):].strip() in TERMINAL else 0.0
    return epoch(t.get("updated") or t.get("created"))


def windows():
    """{name: (window id, pane pid)} in tmux session main."""
    p = sh("tmux", "list-windows", "-t", "main", "-F", "#{window_id}\t#{window_name}\t#{pane_pid}", timeout=20)
    out = {}
    for ln in (p.stdout.splitlines() if p is not None and p.returncode == 0 else []):
        f = ln.split("\t")
        if len(f) >= 2 and f[0] and f[1]:
            out[f[1]] = (f[0], f[2] if len(f) > 2 else "")
    return out


def pane_bare(wid):
    """The pane's shell has no child: nothing is running in there. Not proven bare = not bare."""
    p = sh("tmux", "list-panes", "-t", wid, "-F", "#{pane_pid}", timeout=20)
    pid = ((p.stdout if p is not None else "").splitlines() or [""])[0].strip()
    if not pid:
        return False
    q = sh("pgrep", "-P", pid, timeout=20)
    return q is not None and q.returncode != 0


def pr_states(repo, net=True):
    """{branch: (STATE, merged_at)} from one `gh pr list`; None when GitHub could not be asked."""
    cwd = f"{DEV}/{repo}"
    if not net or not shutil.which("gh") or not os.path.isdir(cwd):
        return None
    p = sh("gh", "pr", "list", "--state", "all", "--limit", str(SWEEP_PRS), "--json",
           "number,state,headRefName,mergedAt", cwd=cwd, timeout=60)
    try:
        rows = json.loads(p.stdout) if p is not None and p.returncode == 0 else None
    except Exception:
        rows = None
    if rows is None:
        return None
    out = {}
    for r in rows:                                      # newest first: an older PR on the branch never overwrites
        out.setdefault(r.get("headRefName") or "", (str(r.get("state", "")).upper(), epoch(r.get("mergedAt"))))
    return out


def pr_of(prs, branch):
    """('?', 0.0) when GitHub could not be asked; (None, 0.0) when the branch has no PR."""
    return ("?", 0.0) if prs is None else (prs.get(branch) or (None, 0.0))


def remote_tracks(repo):
    """The track/* branches on origin, or None when origin could not be listed."""
    p = sh("git", "-C", f"{DEV}/{repo}", "ls-remote", "--heads", "origin", "refs/heads/track/*", timeout=60)
    if p is None or p.returncode != 0:
        return None
    return [ln.split("refs/heads/")[-1] for ln in p.stdout.splitlines() if "refs/heads/track/" in ln]


def newest_write(path):
    """The last mtime anywhere below a directory (links measured, not followed), or None when it is not there."""
    try:
        newest = os.lstat(path).st_mtime
    except OSError:
        return None
    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(path, onerror=lambda e: None):
        for name in dirs + files:
            try:
                newest = max(newest, os.lstat(os.path.join(root, name)).st_mtime)
            except OSError:
                continue
    return newest


def local_only(repo_dir, head):
    """(commits `head` carries that no remote ref reaches, when the newest was committed); (-1, 0.0) = git would not say."""
    if not head:
        return (0, 0.0)
    p = sh("git", "-C", repo_dir, "log", "--format=%ct", head, "--not", "--remotes", timeout=120)
    if p is None or p.returncode != 0:
        return (-1, 0.0)
    ts = [float(x) for x in p.stdout.split() if x.strip().isdigit()]
    return (len(ts), max(ts) if ts else 0.0)


def agent_worktrees(repo):
    """Rule 9's candidates: the worktrees registered directly under <repo>/.claude/worktrees, measured."""
    dev = os.path.realpath(f"{DEV}/{repo}")
    p = sh("git", "-C", dev, "worktree", "list", "--porcelain", timeout=120)
    if p is None or p.returncode != 0:
        return []
    rows, cur = [], {}
    for line in p.stdout.splitlines() + [""]:
        if not line.strip():
            if cur.get("worktree"):
                rows.append(cur)
            cur = {}
            continue
        k, _, v = line.partition(" ")
        cur[k] = v
    hits = []
    for w in rows:
        path = w["worktree"].rstrip("/")
        if os.path.dirname(path) != f"{dev}/{AGENT_WT}":
            continue
        written = newest_write(path)
        if written is None:
            continue
        local, newest = local_only(dev, w.get("HEAD") or "")
        hits.append({"path": path, "name": os.path.basename(path), "idle": max(0.0, now() - written),
                     "branch": (w.get("branch") or "").replace("refs/heads/", ""),
                     "dirty": dirty(path), "local": local, "newest": newest})
    return hits


def held_by(path):
    """Why a live process holds <path>: its cwd, exe or an open file is inside it. [] when nothing does."""
    d, out = os.path.realpath(path).rstrip("/"), []
    for pd in glob.glob("/proc/[0-9]*"):
        pid = os.path.basename(pd)
        links = [f"{pd}/cwd", f"{pd}/exe"]
        try:
            links += [f"{pd}/fd/{fd}" for fd in os.listdir(f"{pd}/fd")]
        except OSError:
            pass
        for ln in links:
            try:
                p = os.path.realpath(os.readlink(ln))
            except OSError:
                continue
            if p == d or p.startswith(d + "/"):
                out.append(f"pid {pid} holds {os.path.basename(ln) if '/fd/' not in ln else 'an open file'} in it")
                break
    return out


def track_verdict(f):
    """Rule 1, pure: {status, age, dirty, snap} → (rm|report|keep, why)."""
    if f["status"] not in TERMINAL or f["age"] <= f.get("stale", STALE):
        return ("keep", "")
    snap = f.get("snap")
    if snap and snap.get("live"):
        return ("report", "still alive — a session is in it")
    if snap and snap.get("state") not in TERMINAL:
        return ("report", f"the board says {f['status']}, the snapshot says {snap.get('state')}")
    if f["dirty"]:
        return ("report", "uncommitted changes in its worktree")
    return ("rm", f"{f['status']} for {dur(f['age'])}")


def branch_verdict(f):
    """Rule 2, pure: {board, pr, dirty} → (delete|report|keep, why). Only MERGED is proof."""
    if f["board"] and f["board"] not in TERMINAL:
        return ("keep", "")
    if f["dirty"]:
        return ("report", "its worktree has uncommitted changes")
    if f["pr"] == "MERGED":
        return ("delete", "its PR is merged")
    if f["pr"] in ("OPEN", "CLOSED"):
        return ("report", f"its PR is {f['pr'].lower()}")
    return ("report", "its PR state could not be read" if f["pr"] == "?" else "no PR was ever opened for it")


def window_verdict(f):
    """Rules 3 and 4, pure: {board, bare} → (kill|report|keep, why)."""
    if f["board"] and f["board"] not in TERMINAL:
        return ("keep", "")
    if not f["bare"]:
        return ("report", "a live process is still in it")
    return ("kill", "a bare shell on a track that is " + (f["board"] or "not on the board"))


def agent_wt_verdict(f):
    """Rule 9, pure: {idle, dirty, local, newest, pr, merged, branch, hours} → (rm|report|keep, why)."""
    if f["hours"] <= 0 or f["idle"] < f["hours"] * 3600:
        return ("keep", "")
    if f["dirty"]:
        return ("report", "uncommitted work in it")
    if f["local"] < 0:
        return ("report", "git would not say whether it holds commits no remote has")
    if f["local"] and (f["pr"] != "MERGED" or not f["merged"] or f["newest"] >= f["merged"]):
        return ("report", f"{f['local']} commit{'' if f['local'] == 1 else 's'} on no remote"
                          + (" that its merged PR does not contain" if f["pr"] == "MERGED" else ""))
    return ("rm", f"nothing has written to it for {dur(f['idle'])}" + (f", and it holds {f['branch']}" if f["branch"] else ""))


class Sweep:
    """One sweep: the dry flag and the tally; every rule logs the same way."""

    def __init__(self, dry=False):
        self.dry, self.did, self.said = dry, [], []

    def log(self, repo, verb, target, why):
        print(f"  {'would ' if self.dry else ''}{verb} {target} — {why}")
        if self.dry:
            return
        try:
            os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
            with open(JANITOR_LOG, "a") as f:
                f.write(f"{stamp()} {repo} {verb} {target} — {why}\n")
        except OSError:
            pass

    def act(self, repo, verb, target, why, run):
        if self.dry:
            self.log(repo, verb, target, why); self.did.append(target)
            return True
        p = sh(*run, timeout=300)
        if p is not None and p.returncode == 0:
            self.log(repo, verb, target, why); self.did.append(target)
            return True
        err = (p.stderr or p.stdout).strip().splitlines()[-1] if p is not None and (p.stderr or p.stdout).strip() \
            else ("no answer" if p is None else f"exit {p.returncode}")
        self.report(repo, target, f"{verb} failed: {err}")
        return False

    def report(self, repo, target, why):
        self.said.append((target, why))
        self.log(repo, "report", target, why)


def agent_hours():
    v = setting("CC_JANITOR_AGENT_HOURS", str(AGENT_HOURS)).strip()
    try:
        return max(0.0, float(v)) if v else 0.0
    except ValueError:
        return AGENT_HOURS


def sweep_repo(repo, r, snap, net=True, stale=STALE):
    """One repo: rules 1-4, then 9. `snap` is this pass's {"repo/track": row}; None = no liveness known, report only."""
    if paused(repo):
        print(f"cc-reconcile sweep {repo}: paused — skipped (cc-pause off {repo})")
        return
    print(f"cc-reconcile sweep {repo}{' (dry run)' if r.dry else ''}")
    try:
        d = board_read(f"{BOARDS}/{repo}.json")
    except Exception:
        d = None
    if d is None:
        r.report(repo, repo, "no board — nothing to sweep")
        return
    no_snap = snap is None
    snap = snap or {}
    for track, t in sorted((d.get("tracks") or {}).items()):        # 1 — terminal tracks
        wt = t.get("worktree") or f"{WTS}/{repo}/{track}"
        st = t.get("status", "")
        verdict, why = track_verdict({"status": st, "age": max(0.0, now() - terminal_since(d, track, t)),
                                      "snap": snap.get(f"{repo}/{track}"), "stale": stale,
                                      "dirty": dirty(wt) if st in TERMINAL else False})
        if verdict == "rm" and no_snap:
            verdict, why = "report", f"would rm ({why}) — held: no liveness snapshot this pass"
        if verdict == "rm":
            wid = (windows().get(f"{repo}/{track}") or ("",))[0]
            if wid and not pane_bare(wid):
                verdict, why = "report", "would rm — held: its window is running something"
        if verdict == "rm":
            spared = held_by(wt) if os.path.isdir(wt) else []
            if spared:
                verdict, why = "report", f"spared {wt}: " + "; ".join(spared)
        if verdict == "rm":
            r.act(repo, "rm", f"{repo}/{track}", why, [sib("cc"), "rm", repo, track])
        elif verdict == "report":
            r.report(repo, f"{repo}/{track}", why)
    try:                                                              # 2 — remote branches (rule 1 took rows off the board)
        d = board_read(f"{BOARDS}/{repo}.json") or d
    except Exception:
        pass
    tracks = d.get("tracks") or {}
    branches, prs = remote_tracks(repo), pr_states(repo, net)
    if branches is None:
        if not os.path.exists(f"{DEV}/{repo}/.cc/member-workspace"):   # a member workspace has no origin by design
            r.report(repo, f"origin/{repo}", "origin could not be listed — no branch was touched")
    else:
        for b in sorted(branches):
            track = b[len("track/"):]
            t = tracks.get(track) or {}
            verdict, why = branch_verdict({"board": t.get("status", ""), "pr": pr_of(prs, b)[0],
                                           "dirty": dirty(t.get("worktree") or f"{WTS}/{repo}/{track}")})
            if verdict == "delete":
                r.act(repo, "delete", f"origin/{b}", why, ["git", "-C", f"{DEV}/{repo}", "push", "origin", "--delete", b])
            elif verdict == "report":
                r.report(repo, f"origin/{b}", why)
    for name, (wid, _) in windows().items():                          # 3 and 4 — windows; `<repo>` itself is never one
        if not name.startswith(f"{repo}/"):
            continue
        track = name[len(repo) + 1:]
        track = track[:-len(NEXT)] if track.endswith(NEXT) else track
        if not track:
            continue
        alive = (snap.get(f"{repo}/{track}") or {}).get("live")
        verdict, why = window_verdict({"board": (tracks.get(track) or {}).get("status", ""),
                                       "bare": not alive and pane_bare(wid)})
        if verdict == "kill":
            r.act(repo, "kill", f"window {name}", why, ["tmux", "kill-window", "-t", wid])
        elif verdict == "report":
            r.report(repo, f"window {name}", why)
    hours = agent_hours()                                             # 9 — subagent worktrees inside the checkout
    for w in agent_worktrees(repo):
        state, merged = pr_of(prs, w["branch"])
        verdict, why = agent_wt_verdict(dict(w, pr=state, merged=merged, hours=hours))
        if verdict == "rm":
            spared = held_by(w["path"])
            if spared:
                verdict, why = "report", f"spared {w['path']}: " + "; ".join(spared)
        if verdict == "rm":
            r.act(repo, "rm", f"worktree {w['path']}", why, ["git", "-C", f"{DEV}/{repo}", "worktree", "remove", w["path"]])
        elif verdict == "report":
            r.report(repo, f"worktree {w['path']}", why)


def fixture_pid(name):
    m = re.fullmatch(r"selftest-(\d+)", name)
    return int(m.group(1)) if m else ccboard().suite_pid(name)


def sweep_fixtures(r):
    """Rule 6, box-wide: every `_cc<suite><pid>` thing whose suite pid is gone — boards, worktrees, state, clones,
    scratch dirs, ledger entries, windows, handoff-ledger lines. Held by a live process → reported."""
    found, fx = {}, ccboard().FIXTURE
    for pat in (f"{BOARDS}/{fx}*", f"{WTS}/{fx}*", f"{STATE}/{fx}*", f"{DEV}/{fx}*",
                f"{HOME}/.cc/selftest-[0-9]*", f"{STATE}/land/{fx}*.applied", f"{HOME}/.claude/projects/{fx}*"):
        for p in glob.glob(pat):
            pid = fixture_pid(os.path.basename(p))
            if pid is not None:
                found.setdefault(pid, []).append(p)
    wins = [(wid, name, fixture_pid(name)) for name, (wid, _) in windows().items() if fixture_pid(name) is not None]
    for _, _, pid in wins:
        found.setdefault(pid, [])
    ledger_f = f"{STATE}/context/handoff.log"
    try:
        lines = open(ledger_f, errors="replace").read().splitlines(keepends=True)
    except OSError:
        lines = []

    def line_pid(ln):
        m = ccboard().SUITE.search(ln)
        return int(m.group(1)) if m else None
    for ln in lines:
        if line_pid(ln) is not None:
            found.setdefault(line_pid(ln), [])
    dead = sorted(pid for pid in found if not os.path.exists(f"/proc/{pid}"))
    if not dead:
        return
    print(f"cc-reconcile sweep: selftest fixtures{' (dry run)' if r.dry else ''}")
    swept = []
    for pid in dead:
        why = f"left by selftest run {pid}, which is gone"
        spared = [s for p in sorted(found[pid]) for s in held_by(p)]
        if spared:
            r.report("selftest", f"selftest run {pid}", "spared: " + "; ".join(spared[:3]))
            continue
        swept.append(pid)
        for p in sorted(found[pid]):
            r.act("selftest", "rm", p, why, ["rm", "-rf", "--", p])
        for wid, name, wpid in wins:
            if wpid == pid:
                r.act("selftest", "kill window", f"{name} ({wid})", why, ["tmux", "kill-window", "-t", wid])
    keep = [ln for ln in lines if line_pid(ln) not in swept]
    if len(keep) < len(lines) and not r.dry:
        try:
            with open(ledger_f + ".tmp", "w") as f:
                f.writelines(keep)
            os.replace(ledger_f + ".tmp", ledger_f)
            r.log("selftest", "scrub", ledger_f, f"{len(lines) - len(keep)} lines of selftest runs that are gone")
        except OSError as e:
            r.report("selftest", ledger_f, f"scrub failed: {e}")


def sweep_cmd(argv):
    """`sweep [<repo>…|--configured] [--dry]`: the repos' rules 1-4 and 9, then the box-wide fixture rule."""
    dry, net = "--dry" in argv, "--no-net" not in argv
    repos = [a for a in argv if not a.startswith("-")]
    if "--configured" in argv:
        repos = setting("CC_JANITOR_REPOS").split()
        if not repos:
            print("cc-reconcile sweep: no repos configured (CC_JANITOR_REPOS in ~/.cc/config) — no repo swept")
    elif not repos:
        print("usage: cc-reconcile sweep <repo> [<repo> …] [--dry] | --configured [--dry]", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    for repo in repos:
        if "/" in repo or repo.startswith(".") or not os.path.exists(f"{BOARDS}/{repo}.json"):
            print(f"cc-reconcile sweep: no board for '{repo}'", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    r = Sweep(dry)
    snap = {f"{rp}/{tr}": {"state": effective(f, decide(f)), "live": bool(f["live"] or f.get("agent_live"))}
            for rp, tr, _, f in facts(repos, net=False, no_stop=True)}
    for repo in repos:
        sweep_repo(repo, r, snap, net)
    sweep_fixtures(r)
    print(f"cc-reconcile sweep: {len(r.did)} swept, {len(r.said)} reported"
          f"{' (dry run — nothing changed)' if dry else f' · log {JANITOR_LOG}'}")
    return 0


# ── the wake ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def tier_allows(what, row=""):
    """`cc-tier allows <what> [<row>]`: exit 1 is "wait"; anything else, or no answer, is "go"."""
    p = sh(sib("cc-tier"), "allows", what, *([row] if row else []), timeout=10)
    return p is None or p.returncode != 1


def live_session(pane_pid):
    """An interactive `claude` anywhere under the pane's shell (a grandchild counts; a headless -p does not)."""
    p = sh("ps", "-eo", "pid=,ppid=,comm=", timeout=20)
    if p is None or p.returncode != 0:
        return False
    kids, name = {}, {}
    for ln in p.stdout.splitlines():
        f = ln.split(None, 2)
        if len(f) == 3:
            kids.setdefault(f[1], []).append(f[0])
            name[f[0]] = f[2].strip()
    seen, stack = set(), list(kids.get(str(pane_pid), []))
    while stack:
        pid = stack.pop()
        if pid in seen:
            continue
        seen.add(pid)
        if name.get(pid) == "claude":
            try:
                argv = open(f"/proc/{pid}/cmdline", "rb").read().split(b"\0")
            except OSError:
                argv = []
            if b"-p" not in argv and b"--print" not in argv:
                return True
        stack.extend(kids.get(pid, []))
    return False


def last_look(repo):
    """The look the seat was last woken for — one line per half of that wake's note — and when it was written."""
    f = f"{STATE}/{repo}/pulse.look"
    try:
        return open(f).read().strip(), os.path.getmtime(f)
    except OSError:
        return "", 0.0


def set_look(repo, look):
    """The state the seat was last woken for; "" forgets it (nobody is there to have heard it)."""
    f = f"{STATE}/{repo}/pulse.look"
    try:
        if not look:
            os.remove(f)
            return
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(f), exist_ok=True)
        open(f, "w").write(look + "\n")
    except OSError:
        pass


def pulse_log(repo, verb, msg):
    print(f"  {repo:<24} {verb:<6} {msg}")
    try:
        os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
        with open(PULSE_LOG, "a") as f:
            f.write(f"{stamp()} {repo} {verb} — {msg}\n")
    except OSError:
        pass


def wake_repo(repo, rows, snap, net, on):
    """One repo: wake its seat when a queued row could start or a row is blocked, once per state per QUIET_H."""
    rows = {k: v for k, v in (rows or {}).items() if isinstance(v, dict)}
    if not rows or all((v.get("kind") or "track") == "session" for v in rows.values()):
        return                                          # a channel repo: its sessions are driven by their channel
    if not on:                                          # cc-pulse.timer was installed off: switching the wake on is the owner's call
        return pulse_log(repo, "skip", "the wake is off — CC_WAKE=on in ~/.cc/config switches it on")
    if paused(repo):
        return pulse_log(repo, "skip", f"paused — `cc-pause off {repo}` puts the whole project back")
    if os.path.exists(f"{STATE}/{repo}/pulse.off"):        # cc-handoff's overlap mark, or one a person touched
        return pulse_log(repo, "skip", "pulse.off — this target has opted out of the wake")
    if not tier_allows("pulse"):
        return pulse_log(repo, "skip", "the spend tier holds the wake — nobody is woken or started")
    words = {k: ((snap.get(f"{repo}/{k}") or {}).get("state") or v.get("status") or "queued",
                 bool((snap.get(f"{repo}/{k}") or {}).get("agent")),
                 bool(str((snap.get(f"{repo}/{k}") or v).get("held") or "").strip()))
             for k, v in rows.items() if (v.get("kind") or "track") != "session"}
    # …AND NOT A ROW INSIDE A LIVE BUNDLE. cc-bundle runs several queued rows as one worker: the bundle row is what is
    # running, and each member stays `queued` with `bundle: <row>` so the bundle's PR can close it. The same test
    # cc-brief's candidates() makes, so the wake and `cc-brief ready` never disagree about it.
    def bundled(k):
        b = str(rows[k].get("bundle") or "").strip()
        return b in words and words[b][0] in ("queued", "running", "waiting", "review")
    due = sorted(k for k, (w, a, h) in words.items() if w in BOARD_DUE and not a and not h and not bundled(k))
    due = [k for k in due if tier_allows("start", f"{repo}/{k}")]
    stopped = [k for k in due if words[k][0] == "blocked"]
    start, could = "none", ""
    if due and net:                                     # the one network call: cc-brief's room arithmetic
        lim = sh(sib("cc-limit"), "status", timeout=30)
        if lim is not None and lim.returncode == 0 and "(this run only)" not in (lim.stdout or ""):
            could = f"{len(due)} queued row(s), none can start — the box is on a usage limit"
        else:
            out = sh(sib("cc-brief"), "ready", repo, *due, timeout=120)
            if out is None or out.returncode != 0:
                start, could = "unread", "cc-brief ready could not say which rows could start"
            else:
                head = ((out.stdout or "").strip().splitlines() or [""])[0]
                could = head.split(": ", 1)[1] if ": " in head else ""
                start = "free" if "could start now" in could else "withheld" if could else "none"
    if not stopped and start not in ("free", "withheld", "unread"):
        return pulse_log(repo, "skip", "nothing a seat can act on")
    # ONE LOOK PER HALF OF THE NOTE, not one per repo. The note below has two halves — which rows have STOPPED, and
    # what `cc-brief ready` said about the QUEUED ones — and each is in the look only when it is in the note. Keyed
    # together, a queued row's verdict flipping tick to tick changed the key and made a long-blocked row read as newly
    # stopped: four wakes of the same seat in three hours for a row that changed nothing (2026-09-20). A wake now needs
    # a half that actually moved; set_look writes both, so a wake for either half re-dates both.
    look = "\n".join(x for x in (f"stopped={','.join(stopped)}" if stopped else "",
                                 f"start={start} due={','.join(f'{k} {words[k][0]}' for k in due)}" if could else "") if x)
    seen, when = last_look(repo)
    if when and now() - when < QUIET_H * 3600 and all(ln in seen.splitlines() for ln in look.splitlines()):
        return pulse_log(repo, "skip", f"woken {int((now() - when) // 60)}m ago for this same state")
    note = " · ".join(x for x in (f"{len(stopped)} row(s) stopped ({', '.join(stopped[:3])})" if stopped else "",
                                  could + (f" (cc-brief ready {repo})" if start != "none" else "")) if x)
    h = sh(sib("cc-handoff"), "--status", repo, timeout=60)     # 0 = a handoff is open, 1 = none, else unknown
    # Only until the cutover: from then `<repo>` is the successor's name and it is live, and a drain of up to ten
    # minutes behind it is no reason to leave a new row unseen for another tick (raised-a-row-for-a-seat-mid-
    # handoff-sits-unseen, 2026-09-23). cc-msg hands the line to cc-slack while the record is open, so it reaches
    # the live side and never the retiring one.
    if h is not None and h.returncode == 0 and "live=successor" not in (h.stdout or ""):
        set_look(repo, "")
        return pulse_log(repo, "skip", "mid-handoff — a successor is taking over")
    w = windows().get(repo)
    if w is None or not live_session(w[1]):
        set_look(repo, "")
        if h is None or h.returncode != 1:
            return pulse_log(repo, "report", "no live session, and cc-handoff could not say whether one is being handed over")
        if not os.path.isdir(f"{DEV}/{repo}"):
            return pulse_log(repo, "skip", f"a board with no ~/dev/{repo} — nothing to start")
        p = sh(sib("cc"), repo, timeout=120)
        if p is None or p.returncode != 0:
            return pulse_log(repo, "report", "could not start a session")
        set_look(repo, look)
        return pulse_log(repo, "start", f"no live session — started one: {note}")
    scr = sh("tmux", "capture-pane", "-p", "-t", w[0], timeout=20)
    if scr is not None and WORKING_FOOTER in (scr.stdout or ""):
        return pulse_log(repo, "skip", "mid-turn — nothing is typed over a turn in progress")
    lim = sh(sib("cc-limit"), "record", w[0], repo, timeout=30)
    if lim is not None and lim.returncode in (0, 2):
        return pulse_log(repo, "skip", "the usage limit stopped it — a line now would only meet the same limit")
    p = sh(sib("cc-msg"), repo, f"wake: {repo} — {note}. Work the board; nothing to act on, reply nothing.", timeout=60)
    if p is None or p.returncode != 0:
        return pulse_log(repo, "report", "wake failed")
    set_look(repo, look)
    pulse_log(repo, "tick", f"live and idle — woken: {note}")


# ── the digest ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def trim(s, n):
    if len(s) <= n:
        return s
    return s[:n].rsplit(" ", 1)[0] + "…"


def few(titles, mx):
    """"a; b; and N more." naming at most mx."""
    titles = [t for t in titles if t]
    s = "; ".join(trim(t, 110) for t in titles[:mx])
    return s + (f"; and {len(titles) - mx} more" if len(titles) > mx else "") + "."


def groups(src, maxg, maxt):
    """One bullet per project, the busiest first; a project past the cap is counted, never dropped."""
    out, order = [], sorted(src, key=lambda rp: (-len(src[rp]), rp))
    for g, rp in enumerate(order):
        if g >= maxg:
            out.append(f"• and {len(src) - maxg} more elsewhere.")
            break
        out.append(f"• {rp}: {few(src[rp], maxt)}" if len(src[rp]) == 1 else f"• {rp}, {len(src[rp])}: {few(src[rp], maxt)}")
    return out


def box_name():
    return setting("CC_BOX") or os.environ.get("CC_BOX") or (sh("hostname", "-s") or subprocess.CompletedProcess([], 1, "", "")).stdout.strip()


def failures_line(named=True):
    """One line from the failure ledger (docs/design-failure-noticing-2026-09-11.md, decision 7): what it holds and
    what crossed the rule — the eligible clusters by kind, three named with episodes and claim word, the rest
    counted; `named=False` (the posted digest) is only how many crossed, and no line when none did. cc-failures owns
    every number; an empty ledger, or a box without one, is '' — no line. Read, never acted on."""
    mp = sh(sib("cc-failures"), "metrics", timeout=30)
    if mp is None or mp.returncode != 0:
        return ""
    m = re.match(r"records: (\d+).*?clusters: (\d+)", (mp.stdout or "").splitlines()[0] if mp.stdout else "")
    if not m or not int(m.group(1)):
        return ""
    recs, cl = int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2))
    ep = sh(sib("cc-failures"), "eligible", timeout=30)
    rows = [ln.split("\t") for ln in (ep.stdout or "").splitlines() if ep is not None and ln.strip()]
    def held(c):   # the claim column, said: "unclaimed 3d 6h" -> "nobody on it for 3 days"
        if not c.startswith("unclaimed"):
            return "someone has taken it"
        sec = sum(int(n) * {"d": 86400, "h": 3600, "m": 60}[u] for n, u in re.findall(r"(\d+)([dhm])", c))
        return f"nobody on it for {spoken_hours(sec)}" if sec else "nobody on it"
    kinds = [f"{r[2].split('/')[-1].replace('-', ' ')} ({r[4].split(' ')[0]} times, {held(r[6] if len(r) > 6 else 'unclaimed')})"
             for r in rows[:3] if len(r) > 4]
    if not named:
        return (f"🧾 {len(rows)} kind{' of failure needs' if len(rows) == 1 else 's of failure need'} a look." if rows else "")
    line = f"🧾 The failure ledger holds {recs} record{'' if recs == 1 else 's'} in {cl} group{'' if cl == 1 else 's'}"
    if not rows:
        return line + ", and none needs a look."
    return (line + f". {len(rows)} happened often enough to need a look: " + "; ".join(kinds)
            + (f"; and {len(rows) - 3} more." if len(rows) > 3 else "."))


def digest_text(snap=None, phone=False):
    """The report: shipped in the window, moving, waiting on you (+ 📌 pins), stopped, held, cost, the failure ledger's line.
    `phone` is the one that is posted: the counts, what waits on him, and one link for the rest."""
    snap = snap_file() if snap is None else snap
    cut = stamp(now() - int(os.environ.get("CC_DIGEST_WINDOW") or 86400))
    ship, move, review, need, stop, held = {}, {}, [], [], [], []
    n = {"q": 0, "bund": 0, "park": 0, "sess": 0}
    for fn, d in boards():
        if d is None:
            continue
        rp = d.get("repo") or os.path.basename(fn)[:-5]
        tracks = {k: v for k, v in (d.get("tracks") or {}).items() if isinstance(v, dict)}

        def in_bundle(v):
            # A QUEUED ROW INSIDE A LIVE BUNDLE IS BEING WRITTEN — by the bundle row, which is what shows under Moving.
            # cc-bundle leaves the member `queued` so the bundle's PR can close it, and marks it `bundle: <row>`;
            # counting it as queued would say the backlog has not moved when it has.
            b = str(v.get("bundle") or "").strip()
            bw = ((snap.get(f"{rp}/{b}") or {}).get("state") or (tracks.get(b) or {}).get("status") or "") if b in tracks else ""
            return bw in ("queued", "running", "waiting", "review")
        for tr, v in sorted(tracks.items()):
            if not isinstance(v, dict):
                continue
            key, ti = f"{rp}/{tr}", str(v.get("title") or tr)
            ti = ti if " " in ti else re.sub(r"[-_]", " ", ti)
            s = snap.get(key) or {}
            st = "session" if (v.get("kind") or "track") == "session" else (s.get("state") or v.get("status") or "?")
            if s.get("waiting_on") == "clock":
                held.append(ti)
                continue
            if st in TERMINAL:
                if str(v.get("updated") or "") > cut:
                    ship.setdefault(rp, []).append(ti)
            elif st == "running":
                move.setdefault(rp, []).append(ti)
            elif st == "review":
                review.append(ti)
            elif st == "waiting":
                need.append((rp, s.get("why") or ti))
            elif st == "blocked":
                stop.append((rp, ti, str(((v.get("notes") or [{}])[-1] or {}).get("msg") or "")))
            elif st == "queued":
                n["bund" if in_bundle(v) else "q"] += 1
            elif st == "session":
                n["sess"] += 1
            else:
                n["park"] += 1
            if os.path.exists(commit_marker(rp, tr)) or os.path.exists(push_marker(rp, tr)):
                stop.append((rp, ti, "the work it is doing is not being saved"))
    n_ship, n_move = sum(map(len, ship.values())), sum(map(len, move.values())) + len(review)
    head = [x for c, x in ((n_ship, f"{n_ship} shipped"), (n_move, f"{n_move} moving"), (len(need), f"{len(need)} waiting on you"),
                           (len(stop), f"{len(stop)} stopped"), (len(held), f"{len(held)} held")) if c]
    spend = ""
    sp = sh(sib("cc-spend"), "today", timeout=60)
    for ln in (sp.stdout.splitlines() if sp is not None and sp.returncode == 0 else []):
        f = ln.split()
        if f[:1] == ["total"] and len(f) > 1:
            try:
                spend = f" ${float(f[1]):.0f} spent" + (f", ${float(f[2]):.0f} with your own sessions" if len(f) > 2 else "") + "."
            except ValueError:
                pass
    out = [f"*{box_name()}* today: {', '.join(head) if head else 'nothing moved'}.{spend}"]
    lp = sh(sib("cc-limit"), "status", timeout=30)
    lim = (lp.stdout or "").strip() if lp is not None and lp.returncode == 0 else ""
    if held and not phone:   # the phone one counts them on the first line and names none
        out.append(f"⏳ Held by the usage limit: {few(held, 4)}" + (f" Claude {lim}." if lim else ""))
    elif lim:
        out.append(f"⏳ Claude {lim}.")
    mp = sh(sib("cc-model"), "status", timeout=30)   # the box off its primary: which KIND (owner, 2026-09-15) — a limit
    ms = (mp.stdout or "").strip() if mp is not None and mp.returncode == 0 else ""   # waits for a reset, "not available" for credits, the cap or a re-login
    if ms and (" until " in ms or "not available" in ms) and not phone:   # the phone one is at its screen budget: `cc-model status` and the whole report carry it
        out.append(f"🔁 Model: {ms} — " + ("not a limit; its sessions are on the next model and return by themselves when it answers again."
                                            if "not available" in ms else "its sessions return by themselves when it lifts."))
    tp = sh(sib("cc-tier"), "line", timeout=10)
    tier = (tp.stdout or "").strip() if tp is not None and tp.returncode == 0 else ""
    if tier and not tier.startswith("The spend tier is autonomous"):   # cc-tier line: "The spend tier is <word>, since <local>. <meaning>."
        out.append("🪫 " + (re.split(r",|\. ", tier)[0] + "." if phone else tier))   # the phone one: the word, not since when or what it means
    fl = failures_line(named=not phone)   # the ledger's one line (#461): what it holds and what crossed the rule, or nothing
    if fl:
        out.append(fl)
    ap = sh(sib("cc-scope"), "digest", timeout=60)
    ask = (ap.stdout or "").strip() if ap is not None and ap.returncode == 0 else ""
    ask = ask.split(" (")[0] if phone else ask   # "91 asks of yours still open", without the breakdown
    if need or ask:
        out += ["", "*Waiting on you*"] + [f"• {rp}: {trim(why, 120 if phone else 240)}" for rp, why in need] + ([ask] if ask else [])
    try:
        pins = json.load(open(os.path.expanduser("~/.cc/slack/revisit.json")))   # HOME at call time: a fixture reads its own pins
        pins = sorted((v for v in pins.values() if isinstance(v, dict)), key=lambda v: -float(v.get("at") or 0))
    except Exception:
        pins = []
    if phone:
        # "fits one phone screen: the counts line, the needs-you items he can act on, one link to the dashboard/canvas
        # for the rest" (brief, 2026-09-12). Every waiting row and the asks line stay above; the rest is named, not listed.
        rest = [x for c, x in ((stop, "why each stopped"), (n_ship or n_move, "what moved"),
                               (pins, f"your {len(pins)} 📌")) if c]
        link = setting("CC_DIGEST_LINK")
        if rest:
            out += ["", f"More on {f'<{link}|the dashboard>' if link.startswith('https://') else 'the Home tab'}: {', '.join(rest)}."]
        return "\n".join(out) + "\n"
    if pins:
        out += ["", "*To revisit* (your 📌)"] + [trim(f"• {v.get('channel') or '?'}: {v.get('text') or ''}"
                                                    + (f" ({v['link']})" if v.get("link") else ""), 240) for v in pins[:4]]
        if len(pins) > 4:
            out.append(f"• and {len(pins) - 4} more: `cc-slack revisit`.")
    if stop:
        out += ["", "*Stopped*"] + [f"• {rp}, {trim(ti, 55)}" + (f": {trim(nt, 110)}" if nt else "") for rp, ti, nt in stop[:3]]
        if len(stop) > 3:
            out.append(f"• and {len(stop) - 3} more.")
    if n_ship:
        out += ["", "*Shipped*"] + groups(ship, 4, 3)
    if n_move:
        out += ["", "*Moving*"] + groups(move, 4, 3) + ([f"• in review: {few(review, 3)}"] if review else [])
    rest = [x for c, x in ((n["q"], f"{n['q']} queued"), (n["bund"], f"{n['bund']} in bundles"), (n["park"], f"{n['park']} parked"),
                           (n["sess"], f"{n['sess']} session{'' if n['sess'] == 1 else 's'} open")) if c]
    if rest:
        out += ["", ", ".join(rest) + "."]
    return "\n".join(out) + "\n"


def digest_post(text):
    """The main lane as a major update (cc-notify would route it to the updates lane); under a harness, the log."""
    if os.environ.get("CC_NOTIFY_LOG_ONLY"):
        try:
            with open(os.environ.get("CC_NOTIFY_LOG") or f"{STATE}/notify.log", "a") as fh:
                fh.write(f"digest\t{text.splitlines()[0] if text else ''}\n")
        except OSError:
            pass
        return
    sh(sib("cc-slack"), "post", "--major", "-c", f"#{box_name()}", text, timeout=60)


def digest_cmd(argv):
    if argv not in ([], ["--notify"]):
        print("usage: cc-reconcile digest [--notify]", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    text = digest_text(phone=bool(argv))   # a person at a terminal reads the whole report; what is posted is the phone one
    sys.stdout.write(text)
    if argv:
        digest_post(text)
    return 0


def retry_requests():
    """A `cc-notify --ask` the broker did not take stays on file under ~/.cc/requests with delivered=false; every tick
    offers each one again (`cc-notify requests --retry`) until the control seat's broker has it. Never a Slack post,
    never the owner: the request is preserved and retried, not dropped and not dumped on him."""
    reqs = os.path.expanduser("~/.cc/requests")           # $HOME at call time: a fixture's, under a selfcheck
    if not any(f.endswith(".json") for f in (os.listdir(reqs) if os.path.isdir(reqs) else [])):
        return
    try:
        subprocess.run([sib("cc-notify"), "requests", "--retry"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        pass


# ── the failure investigation ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
INVESTIGATE_KEY = "CC_FAILURES_INVESTIGATE"   # the owner's one named setting: `cc-config set CC_FAILURES_INVESTIGATE on`


def running_investigation(root="/proc"):
    """True when a `cc-audit failure …` is running on the box. A `claude` whose prompt QUOTES the command is not one."""
    for d in os.listdir(root) if os.path.isdir(root) else []:
        if not d.isdigit() or int(d) == os.getpid():
            continue
        try:
            argv = open(f"{root}/{d}/cmdline", "rb").read().decode(errors="replace").split("\0")
        except OSError:
            continue
        if any(os.path.basename(a) == "claude" for a in argv):
            continue
        if any(os.path.basename(a) == "cc-audit" and argv[i + 1:i + 2] == ["failure"] for i, a in enumerate(argv)):
            return True
    return False


def investigate(dry=False):
    """Claim one eligible failure cluster and launch its investigation (docstring: THE INVESTIGATION). Returns the line
    to print, or None when there is nothing to say. --dry claims nothing and launches nothing: it names the cluster the
    pass would take and what, if anything, holds it. Never raises: a timer pass does not die of this."""
    p = sh(sib("cc-failures"), "eligible", timeout=30)
    n = sum(1 for ln in (p.stdout if p else "").splitlines() if "\tunclaimed" in ln)
    holds, on = [], setting(INVESTIGATE_KEY).lower() == "on"
    # "the launch checks `cc-tier allows explore` and stands down when it says no, the cluster staying eligible and
    # visible with its age" — no claim is taken, so `cc board failures` keeps saying `unclaimed <age>`. No answer from
    # cc-tier holds too (unlike tier_allows): this is the one spend the pass starts on its own.
    t = sh(sib("cc-tier"), "allows", "explore", timeout=10) if on else None
    if not on:
        holds.append(f"{INVESTIGATE_KEY} is not on")
    elif not t or t.returncode != 0:
        holds.append("the tier holds explore work")
    launcher = os.environ.get("CC_RECONCILE_LAUNCH")   # tests: a stub in place of the unit
    # The scan is box-wide, so a stubbed pass skips it unless it names a fixture /proc: the box's own investigation
    # in flight must never hold a fixture's launch.
    proc = os.environ.get("CC_RECONCILE_PROC") or ("" if launcher else "/proc")
    if proc and running_investigation(proc):
        holds.append("an investigation is still running")   # one at a time, never two at once
    if dry:
        c = sh(sib("cc-failures"), "claim", "--dry", timeout=30)
        if not c or c.returncode != 0:
            return f"  investigation  would claim nothing: {(c.stderr.strip() if c else '') or 'cc-failures did not answer'}"
        claim, cluster, scope, kind = (c.stdout.rstrip("\n").split("\t") + ["", "", "", ""])[:4]
        return (f"  investigation  would claim {claim} {scope}/{kind} ({cluster})"
                + (f" — but {'; '.join(holds)}" if holds else " and launch `cc-audit failure` on it"))
    if holds:
        if holds[0].startswith("the tier") and n:
            return f"  held       failure investigation: the tier holds explore work; {n} eligible cluster(s) wait, unclaimed"
        return None                                     # inert until the owner turns it on, or one is still running
    c = sh(sib("cc-failures"), "claim", timeout=30)
    if not c or c.returncode != 0:
        return None                                     # nothing eligible, or the day's slots spent: cc-failures says why
    claim, cluster, scope, kind = (c.stdout.rstrip("\n").split("\t") + ["", "", "", ""])[:4]
    if launcher:
        r = sh(launcher, "failure", claim, timeout=30); how = "stub" if r and r.returncode == 0 else "stub failed"
    else:
        # A transient unit, not a child: this pass is a oneshot service, and a child in its control group dies with it
        # minutes before the model answers — the same reason the lander's queue worker is started this way.
        unit = f"cc-audit-failure-{claim}"
        r = sh("systemd-run", "--user", "--collect", "--quiet", f"--unit={unit}",
               "--description=cc-audit: one bounded failure investigation", sib("cc-audit"), "failure", claim)
        if r and r.returncode == 0:
            how = unit
        else:
            try:
                subprocess.Popen([sib("cc-audit"), "failure", claim], start_new_session=True,
                                 stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
                how = "a detached child (no systemd --user here)"
            except Exception as e:
                how = f"launch failed: {e.__class__.__name__}"
    try:
        os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
        with open(f"{STATE}/reconcile.log", "a") as log:
            log.write(f"{stamp()}\tinvestigation\t{claim} {cluster} {scope}/{kind}\t{how}\n")
    except OSError:
        pass
    return f"  investigation  {claim} {scope}/{kind} ({cluster}) — cc-audit failure launched: {how}"


# ── the deep fix ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DEEP_KEY = "CC_RECURRING_RED_FIX"   # the switch: `cc-config set CC_RECURRING_RED_FIX on`
DEEP_MODEL, DEEP_EFFORT, DEEP_LOOP, DEEP_BUDGET = "claude-opus-5-5", "max", "3", "25"   # the brief: "claude-opus-5-5 at --effort max"


def deep_brief(k):
    """The worker's brief for one claim: goal, why, boundaries, done. The evidence is the claim's own."""
    return (f"GOAL: the gate case below has gone red on {len(k['landings'])} landings of other work, and every PR it "
            f"blocked paid for its own gate runs against it. Find the root cause and open a fix PR against main. If the "
            f"cause is outside this repo (the host, a service, an account), file it with `cc board add {k['scope']} "
            f"raised-<short-name> ...` saying what you found, and stop.\n"
            f"CASE: {k['text']}\nGATE: {k['gate']}\nRED ON: {', '.join(k['landings'][:15])}\n"
            f"EXCERPTS: {' '.join(k['excerpts']) or '(none kept)'}\n"
            f"WHY: one deep read instead of the same red bought again by each landing (claim {k['id']}, case {k['case']}).\n"
            f"BOUNDARIES: fix the cause, not the case's assertion; land through the lane (`cc done`), never merge by "
            f"hand; leave the blocked PRs alone.\nDONE: the case passes on main, or a raised- row names the outside cause.")


def deep_fix(dry=False):
    """Claim one recurring gate red and launch its one worker (docstring: THE DEEP FIX). Returns the line to print, or
    None when there is nothing to say. --dry claims and launches nothing. Never raises."""
    holds, on = [], setting(DEEP_KEY).lower() == "on"
    t = sh(sib("cc-tier"), "allows", "explore", timeout=10) if on else None
    if not on:
        holds.append(f"{DEEP_KEY} is not on")
    elif not t or t.returncode != 0:
        holds.append("the tier holds explore work")
    if not on and not dry:
        return None                                     # inert: not even the ledger is read
    try:
        if dry or holds:
            c = sh(sib("cc-failures"), "recurring", "claim", "--dry", timeout=60)
            if not c or c.returncode != 0:
                why = (c.stderr.strip() if c else "") or "cc-failures did not answer"
                return f"  deep fix   would claim nothing: {why}" if dry else None
            k = json.loads(c.stdout)
            if dry:
                return (f"  deep fix   would claim {k['case']} in {k['scope']} ({len(k['landings'])} landings)"
                        + (f" — but {'; '.join(holds)}" if holds else
                           f" and launch {k['track']} on {DEEP_MODEL} at --effort {DEEP_EFFORT}"))
            return (f"  held       deep fix: the tier holds explore work; case {k['case']} waits, unclaimed"
                    if holds[0].startswith("the tier") else None)
        c = sh(sib("cc-failures"), "recurring", "claim", timeout=60)
        if not c or c.returncode != 0:
            return None                                 # nothing over the threshold, or all held: cc-failures says why
        k = json.loads(c.stdout)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    r = sh(os.environ.get("CC_RECONCILE_DEEP_LAUNCH") or sib("cc"), k["scope"], k["track"], "--go", deep_brief(k),
           "--model", DEEP_MODEL, "--effort", DEEP_EFFORT, "--loop", DEEP_LOOP, "--budget", DEEP_BUDGET, timeout=180)
    if r and r.returncode == 0:
        how = "launched"
    else:
        said = ((r.stdout + r.stderr).strip().splitlines() or ["no output"])[-1][:200] if r else "no answer"
        how = f"launch failed: {said}"
    try:
        os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
        with open(f"{STATE}/reconcile.log", "a") as log:
            log.write(f"{stamp()}\tdeep-fix\t{k['id']} {k['case']} {k['scope']}/{k['track']}\t{how}\n")
    except OSError:
        pass
    return f"  deep fix   {k['id']} {k['scope']}/{k['track']} ({len(k['landings'])} landings) — {how}"


def deep_fix_cmd(argv):
    if argv not in ([], ["--dry"]):
        print("usage: cc-reconcile deep-fix [--dry]", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    line = deep_fix(dry=bool(argv))
    print(line.strip() if line else "deep fix: nothing to launch")
    return 0


def investigate_cmd(argv):
    if argv not in ([], ["--dry"]):
        print("usage: cc-reconcile investigate [--dry]", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    line = investigate(dry=bool(argv))
    print(line.strip() if line else "investigation: nothing to launch")
    return 0


def tick(snap, net):
    """What rides the --apply pass after the reconcile: the fixture rule, the daily sweep, the wake, the daily digest,
    the failure investigation, and the planner requests the broker has not taken yet (core/docs/comms-contract.md:
    "queued" is not "handled")."""
    r = Sweep(False)
    sweep_fixtures(r)
    retry_requests()
    inv = investigate()
    if inv:
        print(inv)
    deep = deep_fix()
    if deep:
        print(deep)
    sw = f"{STATE}/sweep.stamp"
    try:
        due = now() - os.path.getmtime(sw) > 86400
    except OSError:
        due = True
    if due:
        for repo in setting("CC_JANITOR_REPOS").split():
            if os.path.exists(f"{BOARDS}/{repo}.json"):
                sweep_repo(repo, r, snap, net)
        os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
        open(sw, "w").close()
    wake = setting("CC_WAKE") == "on"
    for fn, d in boards():
        if d is not None:
            wake_repo(d.get("repo") or os.path.basename(fn)[:-5], d.get("tracks") or {}, snap, net, wake)
    try:                                                # the zone is named: a bare 11:00 moves when the host's zone does
        at = datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(now(), zoneinfo.ZoneInfo(DIGEST_TZ))
    except zoneinfo.ZoneInfoNotFoundError:              # no tz database: the host's clock rather than no digest
        at = datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(now())
    ds, today = f"{STATE}/digest.stamp", at.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
    try:
        posted = open(ds).read().strip()
    except OSError:
        posted = ""
    if at.hour >= DIGEST_HOUR and posted != today:
        # No longer posted: the owner reads the Home tab, and a debugging engineer reads the boards/logs this
        # digest would have summarized. The stamp still marks the day it ran, so a second tick the same day
        # is still a no-op — `digest --notify` (a person asking for it by hand) still posts.
        open(ds, "w").write(today + "\n")


def main(argv):
    if argv[:1] == ["selfcheck"]:
        return selfcheck()
    if argv[:1] == ["view"]:
        return view()
    if argv[:1] == ["sweep"]:
        return sweep_cmd(argv[1:])
    if argv[:1] == ["digest"]:
        return digest_cmd(argv[1:])
    if argv[:1] == ["investigate"]:
        return investigate_cmd(argv[1:])
    if argv[:1] == ["deep-fix"]:
        return deep_fix_cmd(argv[1:])
    snap_only = argv[:1] == ["snapshot"]
    if snap_only:
        argv = argv[1:] + ["--no-net"]
        if any(a in ("--apply", "--notify") for a in argv):
            print("cc-reconcile: snapshot writes nothing — it takes no --apply or --notify", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    repos, apply_, notify, as_json, quiet, net, grace, repeat = [], False, False, False, False, True, GRACE, REPEAT
    no_stop, wedged = False, int(os.environ.get("CC_RECONCILE_WEDGED") or WEDGED)
    mark = float(os.environ.get("CC_AGENT_MARK_HOURS") or AGENT_MARK / 3600) * 3600
    pend_after = int(os.environ.get("CC_PENDING_ALERT") or PENDING)
    while argv:
        a = argv.pop(0)
        if a == "--apply":
            apply_ = True
        elif a == "--no-stop":
            no_stop = True
        elif a == "--notify":
            notify = True
        elif a == "--json":
            as_json = True
        elif a in ("-q", "--quiet"):
            quiet = True
        elif a == "--no-net":
            net = False
        elif a in ("--grace", "--repeat"):
            if not argv or not argv[0].lstrip("-").isdigit():
                print(f"cc-reconcile: {a} needs a number of seconds", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
            v = int(argv.pop(0))
            grace, repeat = (v, repeat) if a == "--grace" else (grace, v)
        elif a in ("-h", "--help"):
            print(__doc__.strip())
            return 0
        elif a.startswith("-"):
            print(f"cc-reconcile: unknown option {a}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        else:
            repos.append(a)
    for r in repos:
        if not os.path.exists(f"{BOARDS}/{r}.json"):
            print(f"cc-reconcile: no board for '{r}'", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    recs, tracks, wedging, snaprows = [], 0, {}, []
    for repo, track, t, f in facts(repos, net, grace, no_stop, wedged, mark):
        tracks += 1
        if f.get("wedged_now"):
            wedging[f"{repo}/{track}"] = now()
        mine = decide(f)
        state = effective(f, mine)
        who, why = waits_for(f) if state not in TERMINAL else ("", "")
        snaprows.append((repo, track, f, state, who, why))
        for kind, st, why_ in mine:
            rec = {"repo": repo, "track": track, "kind": kind, "from": f["status"], "to": st, "why": why_,
                   "pr": f.get("pr") or ""}
            if kind == "stop":
                rec["pids"] = f["workers"] + f["loops"]
            recs.append(rec)
    if not snap_only:
        ledger(f"{STATE}/wedged.json", wedging)
    for repo, track, (kind, st, why) in orphans(repos, net, grace):
        recs.append({"repo": repo, "track": track, "kind": kind, "from": "", "to": st, "why": why})
    for r in recs:
        if r["kind"] == "stop":
            r["applied"] = bool(apply_ and end_it(r["pids"])
                                and board("status", r["repo"], r["track"], "blocked")
                                and board("note", r["repo"], r["track"], f"stopped by cc-reconcile: {r['why']}"))
            continue
        r["applied"] = bool(apply_ and r["to"] and r["to"] != r["from"]
                            and board("status", r["repo"], r["track"], r["to"])
                            and board("note", r["repo"], r["track"], f"reconciled: {r['from']} → {r['to']} ({r['why']})"))
    if apply_ and any(r["applied"] for r in recs):
        os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
        with open(f"{STATE}/reconcile.log", "a") as log:
            for r in (x for x in recs if x["applied"]):
                what = "STOPPED" if r["kind"] == "stop" else f"{r['from']} -> {r['to']}"
                log.write(f"{stamp()}\t{r['repo']}/{r['track']}\t{what}\t{r['why']}\n")
    snap = snapshot(snaprows, limit_until())
    if snap_only:
        print(json.dumps(snap, indent=2))
        return 0
    if not repos:                                       # a filtered run must never clobber the whole box's snapshot
        try:
            os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
            json.dump(snap, open(f"{STATE}/reconcile.json.tmp", "w"), indent=2)
            os.replace(f"{STATE}/reconcile.json.tmp", f"{STATE}/reconcile.json")
        except OSError:
            pass
        sh(f"{BIN}/cc-trust", "prune", timeout=30)
        # --rotate only under --apply: a bare `cc-reconcile` reports and changes nothing, and the rotation opens
        # a paid successor beside a seat (review of #552). The reaper half runs on every unfiltered run, as before.
        sh(f"{BIN}/cc-handoff", "--sweep", *(["--rotate"] if apply_ else []), timeout=60)
        if net:
            sh(f"{BIN}/cc-slack", "approvals-sweep", timeout=180)
        if apply_:
            import contextlib, io
            with contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO() if quiet or as_json else sys.stdout):
                try:
                    tick(snap["tracks"], net)
                except Exception as e:                  # the tick never fails the reconcile that carried it
                    print(f"  tick failed: {e.__class__.__name__}: {e}")
    asks = [r for r in recs if r["kind"] in ("ask", "stop")]
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({"tracks": tracks, "records": recs}, indent=2))
    elif not quiet:
        for r in recs:
            move = f"{r['from']} → {r['to']}" if r["to"] and r["to"] != r["from"] else ""
            word = {"ask": "needs you", "info": "unknown", "held": "held",
                    "stop": "stopped" if r["applied"] else "runaway"}.get(r["kind"], "fixed" if r["applied"] else "would fix")
            print(f"  {word:<9}  {r['repo']}/{r['track']:<16} {move:<20} {r['why']}")
        info = sum(r["kind"] == "info" for r in recs)
        held = sum(r["kind"] == "held" for r in recs)
        print(" · ".join(x for x in (f"{len(recs) - len(asks) - info - held} {'fixed' if apply_ else 'to fix'}",
                                     f"{len(asks)} needs you", f"{held} held" if held else "",
                                     f"{info} unknown") if x) + f"  ({tracks} tracks)"
              if recs else f"the board matches reality ({tracks} tracks)")
    if notify:
        path = f"{STATE}/reconcile.seen.json"
        old, t0 = ledger(path), now()
        inj = os.environ.get("CC_RECONCILE_INJECT") or f"{BIN}/cc-slack"

        def offer(repo, line):
            p = sh(inj, "inject", "--no-start", repo, line, timeout=30)
            return p is not None and p.returncode == 0

        merged_seen = {}

        def merged_now(repo, pr):
            """The PR read again AT SEND TIME. facts() read it when the run began; the tick (sweep, wake, digest,
            three sibling tools) ran since, and PR #521 merged 16 s before its "review and land it" went out on a
            state read minutes earlier (raised 2026-09-19). One gh call per PR per pass, only for a line about to
            be sent; --no-net never asks, so it never drops. The brief: "a finding re-checks its PR's merge state
            at send time and is dropped if merged"."""
            if not pr or not net:
                return False
            if pr not in merged_seen:
                merged_seen[pr] = pr_state(repo, pr, net) == "MERGED"
            return merged_seen[pr]

        parked = {}

        def project_parked(repo):                       # a parked project is neither nagged nor paged
            if repo not in parked:
                parked[repo] = paused(repo)
            return parked[repo]

        row_facts = {f"{repo}/{track}": f for repo, track, f, _, _, _ in snaprows}

        def merge_answers(r):
            """Does the merge ANSWER this line? Only then is it dropped. Dropping every ask on a MERGED PR took the
            safety asks with it: a `merged` row whose branch really holds commits origin lacks is still reported
            (the invariant up top), and that ask went nowhere while its key was written as 0, so each pass dropped
            it again until the sweep deleted the branch at 48 h with the commits on it. decide() with the PR read
            as MERGED is the test — whatever it still says is not the merge's to answer."""
            if not merged_now(r["repo"], r.get("pr")):
                return False
            f = row_facts.get(f"{r['repo']}/{r['track']}")
            return f is None or not any(w == r["why"] for _, _, w in decide(dict(f, pr_state="MERGED")))

        keys = {f"{r['repo']}/{r['track']}: {r['why']}": r for r in asks if not project_parked(r["repo"])}
        fresh = [r for k, r in keys.items() if t0 - float(old.get(k, 0) or 0) >= repeat
                 and not merge_answers(r)]   # merged since the run began: the next pass fixes the row
        told = {f"{r['repo']}/{r['track']}: {r['why']}" for r in fresh}
        keep, busy = {}, None
        for repo, track, f, state, who, _ in snaprows:  # pending: finished, PR open, nobody landing it
            # A ROW WAITING ON A PERSON HAS BEEN PICKED UP: its seat stood down and asked, and the answer is that
            # person's. "review and land it" is then a full context read the seat can do nothing with (career/
            # positioning PR #4 was offered one every ~2 h while it sat there), and "nobody has picked it up" is
            # not true of it either. Silent like a `held` row, memo and all, so the PR is news again — once — when
            # the answer comes and the row stops waiting.
            if project_parked(repo) or f.get("held") or who == "person":
                continue
            k, ak = f"pending {repo}/{track}", f"alerted {repo}/{track}"
            ok_ = f"offered {repo}/{track} {f.get('pr') or ''}".rstrip()
            if not pending(f, state):
                if state == "review" and f.get("pr_state") == "?":   # one failed poll keeps the clocks
                    keep.update({x: old[x] for x in (k, ak, ok_) if old.get(x)})
                continue
            busy = landing() if busy is None else busy
            if (repo, pr_number(f.get("pr"))) in busy or refused(repo, f.get("pr"), net):
                continue
            first = float(old.get(k) or 0) or t0
            last, stood = float(old.get(ak) or 0), t0 - first
            due = stood >= pend_after and not old.get(ak)   # ak, once set, never fires again — at most ONE notice ever
            if (not old.get(ok_) or due) and merged_now(repo, f.get("pr")):
                continue                                # about to nag, and the PR has merged since facts() read it: nothing
            keep[k] = first                             # to send, no memo, and the next pass marks the row merged
            if due:
                last = t0
                # At most ONE notice per PR, ever: `ak`, once set, gates every later pass off (the `due` check
                # above), so this never fires twice for the same unresolved PR. The age keeps counting in `k`,
                # read by `view`/the dashboard, whether or not this fired.
                alert(f"⏳ {repo}: {row_title(repo, track)} has been waiting to land for {spoken_hours(stood)}, "
                      f"and nobody has picked it up." + (f" {f['pr']}" if f.get("pr") else ""))
            if last:
                keep[ak] = last
            if old.get(ok_):
                keep[ok_] = old[ok_]
            elif offer(repo, f"board watchdog: {repo}/{track}: finished, PR open, not landed — review and land it"
                             + (f" ({f['pr']})" if f.get("pr") else "")):
                keep[ok_] = t0
        if repos:                                       # a filtered run drops no other repo's entries
            keep.update({x: v for x, v in old.items() if x.split(": ")[0].removeprefix("pending ")
                         .removeprefix("alerted ").removeprefix("offered ").split("/")[0] not in repos})
        if keys or keep or old:   # only findings that are still true survive the write: one that comes back is news again
            new = ledger(path, dict({k: (t0 if k in told else old.get(k, 0)) for k in keys}, **keep))
            # …and a nag that just went away is held against the authoritative state at the time it went out: one
            # that the state disproves is a failure, written where it happened (false_nags). `pending` is a clock, not a nag.
            gone = {k: v for k, v in old.items() if k not in new and not k.startswith("pending ")}
            if gone:
                false_nags(gone, {f"{repo}/{track}": f.get("pr") for repo, track, f, _, _, _ in snaprows}, net)
        if fresh:
            # THE SESSION FIRST (owner, 2026-08-31, thread 1788215141): most board-vs-box drift — a finished
            # worker with no PR, a closed PR, a gone worktree — is the live planning session's to fix, not an
            # owner decision. Each finding is offered to that repo's session; the owner is paged only with what
            # no session took (`inject --no-start`: a dead daemon or no session window refuses, and THAT pages).
            # Tradeoff, named: a live session that drops an inject keeps the finding off the owner's phone for
            # the repeat window — the digest still carries the track meanwhile.
            paged = []
            for r in fresh:
                line = f"board watchdog: {r['repo']}/{r['track']} — {r['why']}" + (f" (set to {r['to']})" if r["applied"] else "")
                if not offer(r["repo"], line):
                    paged.append(r)
            if paged:
                one = {r["repo"] for r in paged}
                title = f"{one.pop()} board" if len(one) == 1 else "board"
                body = "\n".join(f"• {r['repo']}/{r['track']} — {r['why']}" + (f" (set to {r['to']})" if r["applied"] else "")
                                 for r in paged)
                sh(f"{BIN}/cc-notify", "-t", title, f"The board did not match the box, and this part needs you:\n{body}", timeout=30)
    return 1 if asks else 0


# ── selfcheck ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def selfcheck():
    """The decision table, then one end-to-end run of each part against a throwaway HOME. No network, no Slack."""
    import tempfile
    global BOARDS                          # declared once, up top: a later read of it must not predate this
    os.environ["CC_LIMIT_RESUMED"] = os.path.join(tempfile.gettempdir(), "cc-reconcile-selfcheck-no-episode")
    p = f = 0

    def ok(name, cond):
        nonlocal p, f
        if cond:
            p += 1
        else:
            f += 1
            print(f"  ✗ {name}")

    def F(**kw):
        d = {"status": "running", "pr": "", "pr_state": None, "live": False, "wt_exists": True,
             "age": 10 ** 6, "grace": GRACE, "journal": (None, ""), "loop_end": "",
             "commit_err": False, "push_err": False, "unpushed": True, "has_remote": True,
             "limited": False, "loops": [], "workers": [], "pane_idle": 0.0,
             "agent": "", "agent_live": False, "agent_stale": "", "held": "",
             "delivery": True, "started": False, "worked": False}   # every existing case below is a row that
        d.update(kw)
        return d

    def one(**kw):
        r = decide(F(**kw))
        return (r[0][0], r[0][1]) if r else ("none", None)

    def eff(**kw):                                      # the ONE word: what a consumer of the snapshot reads
        return effective(F(**kw), decide(F(**kw)))

    ok("live worker in a blocked track → running", one(status="blocked", live=True) == ("fix", "running"))
    ok("…BUT A SESSION SITTING IDLE AT ITS PROMPT IN THE WORKTREE IS NOT A WORKER: `blocked` and `waiting` are a "
       "session's words, and flipping one back to `running` on that presence alone reverted a correction within "
       "minutes, three times over two pulses (a member workspace's row, raised 2026-09-10). The brief: 'a status "
       "a session set is not reverted by decide() while no pane is live' — the word stands, and nothing is asked",
       decide(F(status="blocked", live=True, pane_idle=3 * 3600)) == []
       and decide(F(status="waiting", live=True, pane_idle=3 * 3600)) == [])
    ok("…while a pane moved inside IDLE, a worker or a loop IS work in flight and still flips it — and "
       "`queued`/`todo` is nobody's word, so an idle session in that worktree still makes it running",
       one(status="blocked", live=True, pane_idle=600) == ("fix", "running")
       and one(status="waiting", live=True, pane_idle=600) == ("fix", "running")
       and one(status="blocked", live=True, pane_idle=3 * 3600, workers=[1]) == ("fix", "running")
       and one(status="blocked", live=True, pane_idle=3 * 3600, loops=[1]) == ("fix", "running")
       and one(status="queued", live=True, pane_idle=3 * 3600) == ("fix", "running")
       and one(status="todo", live=True, pane_idle=3 * 3600) == ("fix", "running"))
    ok("…AND A BARE `agent` MARK IS NOT WORK IN FLIGHT EITHER: the re-mark loop keeps `agent_at` fresh for as "
       "long as the seat lives, so a row a session set to `blocked`/`waiting` and left marked was flipped back "
       "to `running` on every pass with no pane in the track's window at all (raised 2026-09-19). The word "
       "stands and nothing is asked; the mark still flips a `queued` row, which is nobody's word",
       decide(F(status="blocked", agent="@3:900", agent_live=True)) == []
       and decide(F(status="waiting", agent="@3:900", agent_live=True)) == []
       and one(status="queued", agent="@3:900", agent_live=True) == ("fix", "running"))
    ok("live worker in a merged track is not un-merged", one(status="merged", live=True, pr="u", pr_state="MERGED") == ("none", None))
    ok("running + no worker, but dispatched seconds ago → left alone", one(age=5, grace=600) == ("none", None))
    ok("journal BLOCKED → waiting, and the owner is asked",
       decide(F(journal=("BLOCKED", "which one?")))[0][:2] == ("ask", "waiting"))
    ok("the blocked question is carried, not summarised", "which one?" in decide(F(journal=("BLOCKED", "which one?")))[0][2])
    ok("journal DONE + merged PR → merged", one(journal=("DONE", ""), pr="u", pr_state="MERGED") == ("fix", "merged"))
    ok("journal DONE + open PR → review", one(journal=("DONE", ""), pr="u", pr_state="OPEN") == ("fix", "review"))
    ok("journal DONE + no PR → asks (nobody opened one)", one(journal=("DONE", "")) == ("ask", "review"))
    ok("loop exit → blocked, with the loop's own reason", decide(F(loop_end="exit 4: stalled"))[0][:2] == ("ask", "blocked"))
    ok("nothing says why → blocked and the owner hears about it", one() == ("ask", "blocked"))
    ok("review + merged PR → merged", one(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="MERGED") == ("fix", "merged"))
    ok("merged + open PR → review", one(status="merged", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN") == ("fix", "review"))
    ok("closed-not-merged PR is never guessed at", one(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="CLOSED") == ("ask", None))
    ok("an unreadable PR state is unknown, not a fix", one(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="?") == ("info", None))
    ok("no network → no PR verdict at all", one(status="review", pr="u", pr_state=None) == ("none", None))
    ok("a missing worktree is reported, not repaired",
       ("ask", None, "its worktree is gone") in decide(F(status="review", wt_exists=False)))
    ok("…but a `review` row whose PR is open is not asked about a worktree it never had",
       not any("worktree" in w for _, _, w in decide(F(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN", wt_exists=False))))
    ok("…while a PR number nobody could confirm silences nothing — only OPEN or MERGED says origin has the branch",
       all(("ask", None, "its worktree is gone") in decide(F(status="review", pr="u", pr_state=ps, wt_exists=False))
           for ps in (None, "?", "CLOSED")))
    ok("…and `running` and `waiting` are asked whatever their PR says — those words claim a worker is in one, so "
       "the word this run lands on must not silence the one the board still carries",
       all(("ask", None, "its worktree is gone") in decide(F(status=s_, pr="u", pr_state="OPEN", wt_exists=False))
           for s_ in ("running", "waiting")))
    ok("a merged track's missing worktree is normal", decide(F(status="merged", wt_exists=False)) == [])
    ok("a track that never started is not missing a worktree — under either word for it, since boards written before "
       "the board spoke `queued` still say `todo`",
       decide(F(status="queued", wt_exists=False)) == [] and decide(F(status="todo", wt_exists=False)) == []
       and decide(F(status="queued", live=True))[0][:2] == ("fix", "running"))
    ok("…AND SO IS ONE `word` MOVED OFF QUEUED BY HAND: a person or session can set any status straight onto a "
       "row (`cc-board status`/`note`), dispatch or not — lessons/tutor-on-a-member-lesson was `queued`, never "
       "claimed, only a task.md and no worktree ever, and a note marking it `blocked` (nothing wrong with "
       "starting) was read as a lost worktree. `delivery` is cc-task's claim record, not the board's word, and "
       "a row nothing ever claimed has none",
       decide(F(status="blocked", wt_exists=False, delivery=False)) == [])
    ok("…BUT A ROW cc-task DID CLAIM keeps being asked about, whatever word it wears now: the claim record "
       "outlives the worktree it was made for",
       ("ask", None, "its worktree is gone") in decide(F(status="blocked", wt_exists=False, delivery=True)))
    ok("…AND SO DOES ONE `cc <repo> <track>` STARTED INTERACTIVELY, EVEN WITH NO CLAIM ON FILE: __run/__runmember "
       "and cc-handoff set the board's `started` flag without ever calling `cc-task claim`, so `delivery` alone "
       "misses this dispatch path — `started` catches it",
       ("ask", None, "its worktree is gone") in decide(F(status="blocked", wt_exists=False, delivery=False, started=True)))
    ok("…AND SO DOES ONE THE LEGACY WORKER PATH RAN, EVEN WITH NEITHER A CLAIM NOR `started` ON FILE: `cc <repo> "
       "<track> --go` predates cc-task claim and never sets the board's `started` flag, but a row it actually "
       "ran left a progress.md or loop.log — `worked` catches it, and the never-claimed `blocked` case above "
       "stays empty",
       ("ask", None, "its worktree is gone") in decide(F(status="running", wt_exists=False, delivery=False, started=False, worked=True)))
    ok("A ROW THAT NEVER RAN IS NEVER STARTED, NOT LOST: no claim, not started, no journal, no worktree — a row made "
       "with its project channel and given `running` by hand — is asked about in ONE line that says nothing was "
       "lost; the same word on a row cc-task did claim keeps 'killed, or the box restarted' AND 'its worktree is "
       "gone' (raised 2026-09-11, a member workspace's row). The brief: reported as never started, not as lost",
       decide(F(status="running", wt_exists=False, delivery=False, started=False, worked=False))
       == [("ask", "blocked", "never started: no claim, no worktree, no journal — the word was set by hand, "
                              "nothing was lost")]
       and [w for _, _, w in decide(F(status="running", wt_exists=False, delivery=True))]
       == ["no worker, and nothing says why (killed, or the box restarted)", "its worktree is gone"])
    ok("…and a cold mark still says what happened to a row nothing else ever ran: the mark's reason outranks "
       "never-started, which outranks lost",
       decide(F(status="running", wt_exists=False, delivery=False, started=False, worked=False,
                agent="@3:900", agent_stale="marked by a live session 6 h ago, mark expired"))
       == [("ask", "blocked", "marked by a live session 6 h ago, mark expired")])
    ok("a refused checkpoint is a finding", any("checkpoint" in w for _, _, w in decide(F(status="review", pr="u", commit_err=True))))
    unp = lambda **kw: any("not pushed" in w for _, _, w in decide(F(status="review", pr="u", **kw)))
    ok("an unpushed branch is a finding: the marker AND commits origin does not have", unp(push_err=True, unpushed=True))
    ok("…but the marker alone is not — a worktree origin already has is not nagged, however old its push.err",
       not unp(push_err=True, unpushed=False))
    ok("…and neither is a branch with work origin lacks but no failed push to say so",
       not unp(push_err=False, unpushed=True))
    ok("…while a branch the box could not judge (never fetched, detached HEAD) keeps the marker's answer, because "
       "silence about a real unpushed branch is the worse of the two", unp(push_err=True, unpushed=None))
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tm:
        os.makedirs(f"{tm}/dev/ws/.cc"); open(f"{tm}/dev/ws/.cc/member-workspace", "w").close()
        ok("a member workspace's failed-push marker is the HOST's own, under ~/.cc/push-state — the file in the "
           "worktree is the member's, and nothing on the host writes or clears it",
           push_marker("ws", "t", tm) == f"{tm}/.cc/push-state/ws/t/push.err")
        ok("…while every other repo keeps it in the worktree, where the hook that writes it clears it",
           push_marker("plain", "t", tm) == f"{tm}/.cc/worktrees/plain/t/.cc/push.err")
        wtd, psd = f"{tm}/.cc/worktrees/ws/t/.cc", f"{tm}/.cc/push-state/ws/t"
        os.makedirs(wtd); os.makedirs(psd)
        def cm():   # the path AND whether it lit, read together: a path captured alone is falsified by the next rm
            p = commit_marker("ws", "t", tm)
            return p, os.path.exists(p)
        cm_none = cm()
        open(f"{wtd}/checkpoint.err", "w").close(); open(f"{wtd}/push.err", "w").close()   # the member's own two
        cm_member, pm_member = cm(), push_marker("ws", "t", tm)
        open(f"{psd}/checkpoint.err", "w").close()
        cm_both = cm()
        os.unlink(f"{wtd}/checkpoint.err")
        cm_host = cm()
        ok("a member workspace's `commit!` is lit by EITHER refusal — the host's under ~/.cc/push-state (what `cc "
           "done` writes) or the member's own in-boundary <wt>/.cc/checkpoint.err, the only place their hook can "
           "write; with neither there is nothing to light and the host's path is what a writer gets",
           cm_none == (f"{psd}/checkpoint.err", False) and cm_member == (f"{wtd}/checkpoint.err", True)
           and cm_both == (f"{psd}/checkpoint.err", True) and cm_host == (f"{psd}/checkpoint.err", True))
        ok("…while the failed push stays the HOST's alone, with the member's own push.err sitting right there and "
           "lighting nothing: theirs is credential-less by design, so it is rewritten every turn and cleared by "
           "nothing on the host, and reading it nagged for ever about a branch the sweep had pushed",
           pm_member == f"{psd}/push.err" and not os.path.exists(pm_member))
        ok("…and every other repo has one place for both, the worktree, where the hook that writes them clears them",
           commit_marker("plain", "t", tm) == f"{tm}/.cc/worktrees/plain/t/.cc/checkpoint.err")
    mrg = dict(status="merged", pr="u", pr_state="MERGED", push_err=True, unpushed=None, commit_err=True)
    ok("a merged row says nothing about its branch, its worktree or its last checkpoint: the merge deleted the "
       "branch, which is success", decide(F(**mrg)) == [] and decide(F(**dict(mrg, wt_exists=False))) == [])
    ok("…and `done` is the other finished word, with no PR to re-read and the same silence",
       decide(F(status="done", push_err=True, unpushed=None, commit_err=True, wt_exists=False)) == [])
    ok("…while a branch that is genuinely unpushed on a row nobody merged still says so",
       any("not pushed" in w for _, _, w in decide(F(status="running", live=True, push_err=True, unpushed=True))))
    for w_ in ("merged", "done"):
        ok(f"a `{w_}` row whose branch really does hold commits origin lacks is STILL told, though the same row is "
           "forgiven a branch the box could not judge — a fact is not a doubt",
           any("not pushed" in w for _, _, w in decide(F(status=w_, push_err=True, unpushed=True)))
           and not any("not pushed" in w for _, _, w in decide(F(status=w_, push_err=True, unpushed=None))))
    ok("…and that holds on the tick the PR merges too, when the row still says `review` and this run says `merged`",
       any("not pushed" in w for _, _, w in
           decide(F(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="MERGED", push_err=True, unpushed=True))))
    ok("…and the tick the PR merges is already finished: that run says `merged` and nothing about the branch",
       decide(F(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="MERGED", push_err=True, unpushed=None))
       == [("fix", "merged", "its PR merged")])
    ok("review with no PR and a remote → asks", any("never opened" in w for _, _, w in decide(F(status="review"))))
    ok("review with no PR and no remote is silent", decide(F(status="review", has_remote=False)) == [])
    ok("a quiet track says nothing", decide(F(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN")) == [])

    ok("a session ALIVE with a question for the owner is waiting, not running — the declaration outranks the pid, "
       "which is the whole bug: five of these said `running` for four hours",
       decide(F(status="running", live=True, journal=("BLOCKED", "which syllabus?")))[0][:2] == ("ask", "waiting"))
    ok("…and it is an ASK, so it reaches him, every run, for as long as the question stands",
       decide(F(status="waiting", live=True, journal=("BLOCKED", "which syllabus?")))[0][0] == "ask")
    ok("a worker BETWEEN ITERATIONS declared nothing and is simply running — not waiting on anyone",
       waits_for(F(live=True, loops=[2], workers=[1])) == ("", "")
       and decide(F(status="queued", live=True, loops=[2], workers=[1]))[0][:2] == ("fix", "running"))
    ok("a loop sitting out a usage limit waits on the CLOCK, not on a person, and never becomes an `ask`",
       waits_for(F(limited=True, loops=[2]))[0] == "clock"
       and [k for k, _, _ in decide(F(status="blocked", live=True, limited=True, loops=[2]))] == ["held"])
    ok("…and the two are told apart by WHO, not by the word `blocked`",
       waits_for(F(journal=("BLOCKED", "ship it?")))[0] == "person"
       and waits_for(F(limited=True, loops=[2]))[0] == "clock")
    ok("a limit standing over a track that is actually WORKING is not the clock's doing",
       waits_for(F(limited=True, loops=[2], workers=[1])) == ("", ""))
    ok("a stood-down track goes back to running by itself once its journal stops saying BLOCKED",
       decide(F(status="waiting", live=True))[0][:2] == ("fix", "running"))
    ok("…and with nobody in the worktree either, `waiting` is reconciled like a stale `running` is",
       decide(F(status="waiting", live=False))[0][:2] == ("ask", "blocked"))
    ok("`waiting` with a PR open is a person's word and survives --apply: reconciling it to `review` would erase it "
       "and the pending watchdog would nag on the next tick anyway (lessons#10; owner, 2026-09-01)",
       decide(F(status="waiting", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN")) == []
       and decide(F(status="waiting", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN", journal=("DONE", ""))) == []
       and decide(F(status="running", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN"))[0][:2] == ("fix", "review"))
    ok("…but the PR MERGING moves it: that is a fact, not a word — and a finish with no PR, or a PR closed "
       "without merging, is still reported, without touching the word",
       decide(F(status="waiting", pr="u", pr_state="MERGED", journal=("DONE", "")))[0][:2] == ("fix", "merged")
       and decide(F(status="waiting", journal=("DONE", "")))[0][:2] == ("ask", None)
       and decide(F(status="waiting", pr="u", pr_state="CLOSED", journal=("DONE", "")))[0][:2] == ("ask", None))
    ok("a merged track is never re-opened by an old question in its journal",
       decide(F(status="merged", journal=("BLOCKED", "old"), pr="u", pr_state="MERGED")) == [])
    ok("STATUS: BLOCKED with no question is still a declaration — it stopped, and only a person restarts it",
       decide(F(journal=("BLOCKED", "")))[0][:2] == ("ask", "waiting"))
    ok("nothing is ever inferred from prose: a journal that merely TALKS about waiting declares nothing",
       waits_for(F(journal=(None, "waiting on the owner for the syllabus"))) == ("", ""))
    ok("the snapshot's word is what decide() would set, not what the board says",
       effective(F(status="running", live=True, journal=("BLOCKED", "q")),
                 decide(F(status="running", live=True, journal=("BLOCKED", "q")))) == "waiting")
    ok("…and the board's own word when nothing disagrees with it",
       effective(F(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN"), []) == "review")
    ok("the snapshot carries who and why, which one status word cannot",
       snapshot([("r", "t", F(status="running", live=True), "waiting", "person", "which syllabus?")])
       ["tracks"]["r/t"] == {"state": "waiting", "board": "running", "kind": "track", "live": True,
                             "waiting_on": "person", "why": "which syllabus?", "idle_for": 0,
                             "loop": False, "agent": False, "held": ""})
    ok("…and the three facts the Home tab and the wake used to read for themselves: a live loop, a live agent mark, "
       "a person's hold — so neither needs a process table, a tmux or a board field of its own",
       {k: v for k, v in snapshot([("r", "t", F(status="queued", loops=[2], agent="@1:9", agent_live=True, held=" mine "),
                                     "running", "", "")])["tracks"]["r/t"].items() if k in ("loop", "agent", "held")}
       == {"loop": True, "agent": True, "held": "mine"})
    ok("`todo` is an older board's word for `queued`, and the snapshot says `queued` — one vocabulary for every reader",
       eff(status="todo") == "queued" and eff(status="queued") == "queued")

    ok("a running row a LIVE session marked as its subagent's work is left alone past the grace, and raises "
       "no ask — the mark is the only thing on the box that says anybody is on it",
       decide(F(status="running", agent="@3:900", agent_live=True, age=10 ** 6)) == []
       and eff(status="running", agent="@3:900", agent_live=True) == "running")
    ok("…and the moment that session's window is gone the mark counts for nothing: the same row is reported "
       "abandoned, exactly as it was before any of this",
       decide(F(status="running", agent="@3:900", agent_live=False))[0][:2] == ("ask", "blocked"))
    ok("a marked row that is still `queued` is running, and says WHOSE — never 'a worker is in its worktree', "
       "which is the one thing that is not true of it; a `blocked` row the mark leaves alone entirely",
       decide(F(status="queued", agent="@3:900", agent_live=True))[0] == ("fix", "running", "a live session is doing it in a subagent")
       and decide(F(status="blocked", agent="@3:900", agent_live=True)) == []
       and decide(F(status="queued", live=True))[0][2] == "a worker is in its worktree")
    ok("…AND IT HAS NO WORKTREE: nothing dispatched it, so there is none to be gone, and the mark has to silence "
       "that rule too — otherwise the row it just made quiet goes back to NEEDS YOU on the same run",
       decide(F(status="queued", agent="@3:900", agent_live=True, wt_exists=False))
       == [("fix", "running", "a live session is doing it in a subagent")]
       and decide(F(status="running", agent="@3:900", agent_live=True, wt_exists=False)) == [])
    ok("A COLD MARK IS REPORTED WITH ITS AGE, not as 'nothing says why': the row IS unattended, and the one "
       "thing worth saying about it is that a session took it 9 h ago and never came back",
       decide(F(status="running", agent="@3:900", agent_stale="marked by a live session 9 h ago, mark expired"))
       == [("ask", "blocked", "marked by a live session 9 h ago, mark expired")])
    ok("…AND IT SAYS IT ONCE. A row marked while `queued` was flipped to `running` by the mark, and that word "
       "outlives the mark: with the worktree rule guarded on a LIVE mark, the same row drew 'mark expired' AND "
       "'its worktree is gone' 6 h later — a second NEEDS YOU line for a row that had none before it was marked",
       decide(F(status="running", agent="@3:900", agent_live=False, wt_exists=False,
                agent_stale="marked by a live session 6 h ago, mark expired"))
       == [("ask", "blocked", "marked by a live session 6 h ago, mark expired")])
    W, T0 = {"@3:900": "r"}, 1000 * 3600
    def stamp(secs_ago): return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(T0 - secs_ago))
    ok("a mark made a minute ago holds the row, and one made past the bound does not — with its age in the "
       "reason, so the run says what happened rather than 'nothing says why'",
       mark_why({"agent": "@3:900", "agent_at": stamp(60)}, W, "r", T0, AGENT_MARK) == (True, "")
       and mark_why({"agent": "@3:900", "agent_at": stamp(9 * 3600)}, W, "r", T0, AGENT_MARK)
       == (False, "marked by a live session 9 h ago, mark expired"))
    ok("…and a mark with no time on it holds nothing, which is every mark written before this: unreadable is "
       "'long ago' here as everywhere else, and the row comes back rather than sitting in flight for ever",
       mark_why({"agent": "@3:900"}, W, "r", T0, AGENT_MARK)[0] is False
       and mark_why({"agent": "@3:900"}, W, "r", T0, AGENT_MARK)[1] == "marked by a live session, but the mark carries no time")
    _rz = T0 - 3600.0       # an episode that BEGAN an hour before this run
    ok("a mark made before a limit that has since lifted is cold whatever its age, and the reason names the "
       "hour so the row says what happened to it",
       mark_why({"agent": "@3:900", "agent_at": stamp(5400)}, W, "r", T0, AGENT_MARK, _rz)
       == (False, "marked before the usage limit that began at "
                  + time.strftime("%H:%MZ", time.gmtime(_rz)) + " — that subagent died with it"))
    ok("…while a mark made DURING the episode, once the box was on the fallback, holds its row: the box did not "
       "stop for the limit, and that subagent is still working",
       mark_why({"agent": "@3:900", "agent_at": stamp(1800)}, W, "r", T0, AGENT_MARK, _rz) == (True, ""))
    ok("…and one made at the START second does not: that is the second the limit was first seen in",
       mark_why({"agent": "@3:900", "agent_at": stamp(3600)}, W, "r", T0, AGENT_MARK, _rz)[0] is False)
    ok("…and with no episode passed in, the age bound is the whole rule, which is what this file did before",
       mark_why({"agent": "@3:900", "agent_at": stamp(5400)}, W, "r", T0, AGENT_MARK) == (True, ""))
    ok("A MARK WHOSE SEAT HAS NOT TAKEN A TURN EXPIRES, however fresh the mark: a session's detached re-mark loop "
       "refreshes agent_at on a liveness poll a stalled seat passes, so an orch seat held its row 29 h without a "
       "turn (raised 2026-09-17). The seat's last turn is read beside the mark: none inside the window expires it "
       "with the hours in the reason; one inside the window holds; and a seat nothing says about keeps the clock "
       "it has, so the re-mark loop and this rule coexist",
       mark_why({"agent": "@3:900", "agent_at": stamp(60)}, W, "r", T0, AGENT_MARK, 0.0, T0 - 7 * 3600)
       == (False, "marked by a live session, but that seat has not taken a turn for 7 h — a re-mark is not a turn, "
                  "mark expired")
       and mark_why({"agent": "@3:900", "agent_at": stamp(60)}, W, "r", T0, AGENT_MARK, 0.0, T0 - 5 * 3600) == (True, "")
       and mark_why({"agent": "@3:900", "agent_at": stamp(60)}, W, "r", T0, AGENT_MARK, 0.0, None) == (True, ""))
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as _sd:
        # seat_turn on a REAL pane-shaped process tree: a shell whose child is a `claude` (a script by that name,
        # so comm reads claude) carrying --session-id, and cc-statusline's per-turn file for that id at a chosen
        # time — the walk, the argv read and the file are all the real thing. Then the seats that actually mark:
        # `cc <repo>` and `cc --orch` start theirs with NO --session-id (review of #538), so a second `claude` with
        # none, alone in its cwd, is found by that cwd — its transcript directory and the per-turn file whose
        # raw.cwd it is — and two such peers in one cwd are None, one never standing in for the other.
        open(f"{_sd}/claude", "w").write("#!/bin/sh\nsleep 30\n")
        os.chmod(f"{_sd}/claude", 0o755)
        for _d in ("sl", "pj", "seatA", "seatB"):
            os.makedirs(f"{_sd}/{_d}")

        def _spawn(args, cwd=None):                     # a pane's shell with a `claude` under it
            px = subprocess.Popen(["bash", "-c", f"{_sd}/claude {args}; true"], cwd=cwd,
                                  stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
            for _ in range(100):                        # until the shell's child has exec'd into `claude`
                try:
                    if any(open(f"/proc/{k}/comm").read().strip() == "claude"
                           for k in open(f"/proc/{px.pid}/task/{px.pid}/children").read().split()):
                        break
                except OSError:
                    pass
                time.sleep(0.05)
            return px
        _seat = _spawn("--session-id selfcheck-seat-1")
        _bare = subprocess.Popen(["sleep", "30"])       # a pane with no session under it
        _alone = _spawn("", cwd=f"{_sd}/seatA")         # no id, the one seat in its cwd
        _peers = [_spawn("", cwd=f"{_sd}/seatB"), _spawn("", cwd=f"{_sd}/seatB")]
        _keep_sl, _keep_pj = os.environ.get("CC_STATUSLINE_DIR"), PROJECTS
        os.environ["CC_STATUSLINE_DIR"] = f"{_sd}/sl"
        globals().update(PROJECTS=f"{_sd}/pj")
        try:
            _none = seat_turn(_seat.pid)
            open(f"{_sd}/sl/selfcheck-seat-1.json", "w").write("{}")
            _t7 = now() - 7 * 3600
            os.utime(f"{_sd}/sl/selfcheck-seat-1.json", (_t7, _t7))
            _got = seat_turn(_seat.pid)
            _cwd_none = seat_turn(_alone.pid)           # no id, nothing written for its cwd yet
            for _d in ("seatA", "seatB"):               # a transcript in each cwd's directory, 7 h old
                _pd = f"{_sd}/pj/" + re.sub(r"[/.]", "-", os.path.realpath(f"{_sd}/{_d}"))
                os.makedirs(_pd)
                open(f"{_pd}/some-session.jsonl", "w").write("{}\n")
                os.utime(f"{_pd}/some-session.jsonl", (_t7, _t7))
            _cwd_tr = seat_turn(_alone.pid)
            _t5 = now() - 5 * 3600                      # a per-turn file for that cwd, newer: the newer wins
            json.dump({"raw": {"cwd": f"{_sd}/seatA"}}, open(f"{_sd}/sl/other-id.json", "w"))
            os.utime(f"{_sd}/sl/other-id.json", (_t5, _t5))
            _cwd_sl = seat_turn(_alone.pid)
            _peer_none = [seat_turn(px.pid) for px in _peers]
        finally:
            os.environ.pop("CC_STATUSLINE_DIR", None) if _keep_sl is None else os.environ.update({"CC_STATUSLINE_DIR": _keep_sl})
            globals().update(PROJECTS=_keep_pj)
            _bare_none = seat_turn(_bare.pid)
            for _px in [_seat, _bare, _alone] + _peers:
                _px.kill()
                _px.wait(timeout=10)
        ok("seat_turn walks the pane's process tree to the `claude` under it, reads the session id off its command "
           "line and answers with cc-statusline's per-turn file for that id: the time that file says, and None "
           "before there is one, for a pane with no session under it, or for no pane — no evidence is None, "
           "never 'long ago'",
           _got is not None and abs(_got - _t7) < 2 and _none is None and _bare_none is None
           and seat_turn("") is None)
        ok("…AND A SEAT WITH NO --session-id IS FOUND BY ITS CWD, the seats that actually mark (`cc <repo>`, "
           "`cc --orch`; review of #538): None before anything is written for that cwd; the newest transcript in "
           "the cwd's directory once there is one; and the per-turn file whose raw.cwd is that cwd when it is "
           "newer — the seat's last turn, whichever file carries it",
           _cwd_none is None and _cwd_tr is not None and abs(_cwd_tr - _t7) < 2
           and _cwd_sl is not None and abs(_cwd_sl - _t5) < 2)
        ok("…while two seats with no id in ONE cwd say nothing about each other: both are None (cc-context's own "
           "'ambiguous cwd → no answer'), so a main seat and an orch sharing a checkout keep their clocks rather "
           "than one hiding behind the other's turns",
           _peer_none == [None, None])
    ok("…while a window that is gone, or is another repo's, is refused BEFORE the clock: there is no live "
       "session to name in the reason, and the row is reported exactly as any unattended row is",
       mark_why({"agent": "@9:900", "agent_at": stamp(60)}, W, "r", T0, AGENT_MARK) == (False, "")
       and mark_why({"agent": "@3:900", "agent_at": stamp(60)}, W, "other", T0, AGENT_MARK) == (False, ""))
    ok("the mark claims a session is alive and nothing else: a declared question still outranks it, and a "
       "merged row is still merged", decide(F(status="running", agent_live=True, journal=("BLOCKED", "q?")))[0][:2] == ("ask", "waiting")
       and decide(F(status="merged", agent_live=True, pr="u", pr_state="MERGED")) == [])
    ok("the snapshot counts a subagent as alive, so `cc ls` and the Home tab say the same thing this run did",
       snapshot([("r", "t", F(status="running", agent="@3:900", agent_live=True), "running", "", "")])
       ["tracks"]["r/t"]["live"] is True)
    P = ["proj\t100\t0\t@1:900", "proj/t1\t101\t0\t@2:900", "proj/t2\t999\t0\t@3:900",
         "proj\t102\t0\t", "other\t104\t0\t@4:900"]
    _live, _idle, _wins = panes(P, {"100", "101", "102", "104"}, {"100", "101"})
    ok("a window an `agent` mark can name is any window a SESSION is in — a planning session's is named for its "
       "repo alone, so the TRACK filter must not decide this, and the name comes back to be checked against it",
       _wins == {"@1:900": "proj", "@2:900": "proj/t1"} and _live == {"proj/t1"})
    _wo = {"@5:900": "proj@dash", "@6:900": "other@dash"}
    _at = {"agent_at": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())}
    ok("an orchestrator's mark holds its own repo's row, and still holds no other repo's",
       mark_why(dict(_at, agent="@5:900"), _wo, "proj", now(), 6 * 3600)[0]
       and not mark_why(dict(_at, agent="@6:900"), _wo, "proj", now(), 6 * 3600)[0])
    _started, _pid, _wid, _fw = False, "", "", {}
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as _ts:
        _sock = os.path.join(_ts, "tmux-%d" % os.getuid(), "default")   # where TMUX_TMPDIR=_ts resolves to
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(_sock), exist_ok=True)
        os.chmod(os.path.dirname(_sock), 0o700)         # tmux refuses a socket dir anyone else can read
        _keep = {k: os.environ.get(k) for k in ("TMUX", "TMUX_TMPDIR")}
        os.environ["TMUX_TMPDIR"] = _ts
        os.environ.pop("TMUX", None)
        def _tx(*a):
            try:
                return subprocess.run(["tmux", "-S", _sock, *a], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20)
            except Exception:                           # no tmux at all, or one that will not answer in time:
                return subprocess.CompletedProcess(a, 1, "", "")   # tmux_live swallows the same, and this case
        try:                                            # then goes RED with the rest — never a traceback
            if _tx("list-sessions").returncode != 0:    # nothing answers on our own socket: ours to make
                _started = _tx("-f", "/dev/null", "new-session", "-d", "-s", "notmain",
                               "-n", "proj@dash", "sleep 600").returncode == 0
            if _started:
                def _ask(fmt):
                    return _tx("display-message", "-p", "-t", "notmain:proj@dash", fmt).stdout.strip()
                _pid, _wid = _ask("#{pane_pid}"), _ask("#{window_id}:#{pid}")
                _fw = tmux_live({_pid}, {_pid})[2]
        finally:
            if _started:
                _tx("kill-session", "-t", "notmain")
            for _k, _v in _keep.items():
                os.environ.pop(_k, None) if _v is None else os.environ.update({_k: _v})
    ok("a real tmux window `<repo>@<alias>` in a session that is NOT `main` is read as that repo's, and its "
       "mark holds the row — an orch lives in a session of its own and every one of its rows turns on this",
       _started and _fw.get(_wid) == "proj@dash"
       and mark_why(dict(_at, agent=_wid), _fw, "proj", now(), 6 * 3600) == (True, "")
       and mark_why(dict(_at, agent=_wid), _fw, "other", now(), 6 * 3600) == (False, ""))
    ok("A CHILD IN THE PANE IS NOT A SESSION: a window left with a `tail -f` or an `htop` in it after the session "
       "exited has one for ever, and a mark on it would keep a row alive for ever — it is live for the TRACK "
       "rule and unusable as a mark, which is the difference the two tests exist for",
       "@4:900" not in _wins and panes(P, {"104"}, {"104"})[2] == {"@4:900": "other"})
    ok("…and a pane whose shell has no child is a leftover window, in neither: `cc` leaves one behind an exited "
       "session (exec bash)", "@3:900" not in _wins and "proj/t2" not in _live)
    ok("the mark carries the tmux SERVER too, because window ids restart at @0 when the server does — a mark "
       "left by a session that died in a reboot must not match whatever window is @1 now",
       "@1:900" in _wins and "@1:901" not in _wins)
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tb:
        _B, _W, _pr, _tl = BOARDS, WTS, procs, tmux_live
        _wp, _stn = window_panes, seat_turn
        globals().update(BOARDS=tb, WTS=tb,
                         procs=lambda: (set(), set(), {"7"}, {}, {}),
                         tmux_live=lambda ppids, sessions=(): (
                             set(), {}, {"@5:900": "agentrepo", "@6:900": "otherrepo", "@7:900": "agentrepo"}),
                         window_panes=lambda: {"@5:900": "5000", "@7:900": "7000"},
                         seat_turn=lambda pid: {"5000": time.time() - 60, "7000": time.time() - 7 * 3600}.get(pid))
        try:
            for tr in ("t2", "t3"):
                os.makedirs(f"{tb}/agentrepo/{tr}")
            _fresh = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(time.time() - 60))
            json.dump({"repo": "agentrepo", "tracks": {
                "t1": {"status": "running", "agent": "@5:900", "agent_at": _fresh, "updated": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"},
                "t2": {"status": "running", "agent": "@6:900", "agent_at": _fresh, "updated": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"},
                "t3": {"status": "running", "updated": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"},
                "t4": {"status": "running", "agent": "@5:900", "agent_at": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z",
                       "updated": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"},
                "t5": {"status": "running", "agent": "@7:900", "agent_at": _fresh, "updated": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"}}},
                open(f"{tb}/agentrepo.json", "w"))
            got = {tr: fa for _, tr, _, fa in facts(["agentrepo"], net=False)}
        finally:
            globals().update(BOARDS=_B, WTS=_W, procs=_pr, tmux_live=_tl, window_panes=_wp, seat_turn=_stn)
        ok("facts() reads the seat behind each mark: t5's mark is a minute old and its window holds a session for "
           "the repo, exactly as t1's — and that seat last took a turn 7 h ago, so the mark holds nothing and the "
           "row is asked about in ONE line naming the hours, while t1's seat turned a minute ago and holds",
           got["t5"]["agent_live"] is False and got["t1"]["agent_live"] is True
           and decide(got["t5"]) == [("ask", "blocked", "marked by a live session, but that seat has not taken a "
                                                         "turn for 7 h — a re-mark is not a turn, mark expired")])
        ok("facts() reads the mark off the board file and calls the row alive, worktree or none — the whole "
           "path, so the field name is under test too and no fixture stands in for the missing worktree",
           got["t1"]["agent"] == "@5:900" and got["t1"]["agent_live"] is True
           and got["t1"]["wt_exists"] is False and decide(got["t1"]) == [])
        ok("A SESSION SPEAKS FOR ITS OWN REPO: a mark naming a window that belongs to another repo holds nothing "
           "open — the board is one file every session can write, and this is the reach it must not give",
           got["t2"]["agent_live"] is False and decide(got["t2"])[0][:2] == ("ask", "blocked"))
        ok("…and an unmarked row is untouched by any of it",
           got["t3"]["agent"] == "" and got["t3"]["agent_live"] is False
           and decide(got["t3"])[0][:2] == ("ask", "blocked"))
        ok("A MARK GOES COLD, and facts() carries the age off the board file to say so — t4's session is the "
           "same live one holding t1 open, and the only difference between the two rows is the clock. ONE "
           "record, not two: the row still has no worktree, and a cold mark must not turn that into a second "
           "finding the row never drew before it was marked",
           got["t4"]["agent_live"] is False and got["t4"]["wt_exists"] is False
           and len(decide(got["t4"])) == 1
           and decide(got["t4"])[0][:2] == ("ask", "blocked")
           and decide(got["t4"])[0][2].endswith("h ago, mark expired"))

    ok("a live pane idle 3 h is `idle`, not running: nothing is happening at it",
       eff(status="running", live=True, pane_idle=3 * 3600) == "idle")
    ok("…and the snapshot says how long, so the tab can print it instead of a stale iteration count",
       snapshot([("r", "t", F(status="running", live=True, pane_idle=3 * 3600), "idle", "", "")])
       ["tracks"]["r/t"]["idle_for"] == 3 * 3600)
    ok("a pane touched 10 min ago is simply running",
       eff(status="running", live=True, pane_idle=600) == "running")
    ok("a worker or a loop alive is work in flight whatever the keyboard shows",
       not idle_session(F(live=True, workers=[1], pane_idle=10 ** 5))
       and not idle_session(F(live=True, loops=[1], pane_idle=10 ** 5)))
    ok("no activity stamp is not evidence of idleness",
       not idle_session(F(live=True)) and eff(status="running", live=True) == "running")
    ok("`idle` never touches what counts as WAITING: a declared question still outranks the keyboard",
       eff(status="running", live=True, pane_idle=10 ** 5, journal=("BLOCKED", "q")) == "waiting")
    ok("…nor what the tool STOPS: an orphan idle at its prompt is still an orphan",
       eff(status="running", live=True, pane_idle=10 ** 5, workers=[1], stop_why="orphan") == "blocked")

    ok("finished with an open PR and nobody landing it is pending",
       pending(F(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN"), eff(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN"))
       and decide(F(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN")) == [])
    ok("an unreadable PR state never nags — `?` is not evidence that work is sitting",
       not pending(F(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="?"), eff(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="?")))
    ok("…nor is a run that never asked: --no-net leaves no PR fact, so nothing nags",
       not pending(F(status="review", pr="u", pr_state=None), eff(status="review", pr="u", pr_state=None)))
    ok("a landed track is not pending", not pending(F(status="merged", pr="u", pr_state="MERGED"), "merged"))
    ok("a track still being worked is not pending",
       not pending(F(status="running", live=True, pr="u", pr_state="OPEN"),
                   eff(status="running", live=True, pr="u", pr_state="OPEN")))
    ok("it is the EFFECTIVE state that counts, not the board's word: a stale `running` over an open PR with "
       "nobody in the worktree is a finished track, and pending",
       eff(status="running", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN") == "review"
       and pending(F(status="running", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN"), eff(status="running", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN")))
    ok("a held row raises nothing a person has to answer: the row that would be reported abandoned says `held` "
       "instead, and the same row unheld is the `ask` it always was",
       [k for k, _, _ in decide(F(status="running", live=False, held="behind #309"))] == ["held"]
       and decide(F(status="running", live=False))[0][:2] == ("ask", "blocked"))
    ok("…and it takes a REASON to hold one: an empty word, or one that is only spaces, holds nothing",
       decide(F(status="running", live=False, held=""))[0][0] == "ask"
       and decide(F(status="running", live=False, held="   "))[0][0] == "ask")
    ok("…the hold carries its reason into what is printed, because a hold nobody can see is the board note this "
       "replaces", decide(F(status="running", live=False, held="behind #309"))[0][2] == "held: behind #309")
    ok("a held row is still RECONCILED — a silent fix keeps the board true about a merged PR, and `held` says so "
       "beside it; the ask is the only thing the hold takes away",
       [(k, s) for k, s, _ in decide(F(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="MERGED", held="behind #309"))]
       == [("fix", "merged"), ("held", None)]
       and eff(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="MERGED", held="behind #309") == "merged")
    ok("…and a RUNAWAY on a held row is still stopped: a hold is a person's word about what to do next, never a "
       "licence to burn tokens with nothing coming out",
       [k for k, _, _ in decide(F(status="running", live=True, held="behind #309", stop_why="orphan"))]
       == ["stop", "held"])
    ok("…and a held row whose branch is not pushed still says so: the sweep deletes that branch at 48 h, and a "
       "hold that muted this would feed the only copy of those commits to `git branch -D`",
       any("not pushed" in w for _, _, w in
           decide(F(status="running", live=False, held="behind #309", push_err=True, unpushed=True)))
       and any("only in the worktree" in w for _, _, w in
               decide(F(status="running", live=False, held="behind #309", commit_err=True))))
    ok("…and a held row's QUESTION still reaches the owner: the person-ask is what puts the row on `waiting`, his "
       "NEEDS YOU list, and a hold is a word about the next move, not an answer to what was asked",
       [(k, s) for k, s, _ in decide(F(status="running", live=True, held="behind #309",
                                       journal=("BLOCKED", "which repo?")))]
       == [("ask", "waiting"), ("held", None)]
       and eff(status="running", live=True, held="behind #309", journal=("BLOCKED", "which repo?")) == "waiting")
    ok("…while a SESSION row is untouched by any of it: a channel is not a task, so it has nothing to hold",
       decide(F(kind="session", status="running", live=True, held="behind #309")) == [])
    ok("…except the one word a PERSON typed: a `waiting` row is never pending, however it is reconciled — landing "
       "is what it is waiting on (lessons#10 was nagged five times; owner, 2026-09-01)",
       not pending(F(status="waiting", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN"), "review")
       and not pending(F(status="waiting", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN"),
                       eff(status="waiting", pr="u", pr_state="OPEN")))

    def W(**kw):
        d = {"orphans": [], "workers": [111], "loops": [222], "limited": False, "idle": 4 * 3600}
        d.update(kw)
        return d

    ok("an orphaned worker — no cc-loop above it — is ended on sight, first sighting and all",
       "no cc-loop above it" in runaway(W(orphans=[111], loops=[]), False))
    ok("a worker under its loop, moving, is left alone", runaway(W(idle=60), True) == "")
    ok("wedged for hours but seen only once → not yet; one run is not two",
       runaway(W(), False) == "")
    ok("wedged for hours and the run before saw it too → ended", "wedged" in runaway(W(), True))
    ok("a loop waiting out a usage limit is waiting, not wedged", runaway(W(limited=True), True) == "")
    import tempfile
    _keep, _p = os.environ.get("CC_LIMIT_STAMP"), tempfile.mkstemp(suffix=".claude-limit")[1]
    os.environ["CC_LIMIT_STAMP"] = _p
    try:
        _t = int(now()) + 3600
        open(_p, "w").write(f"{_t}\tusage limit\t{int(now())}\tclaude-fable-5-1\tdeadbeef\n")
        ok("a stamp ONE run hit leaves the reconciler unlimited: that run's limit is not the box's",
           not limit_active() and limit_until() == 0.0)
        open(_p, "w").write(f"{_t}\tusage limit\t{int(now())}\t\tdeadbeef,cafef00d\n")
        ok("two runs on it make it the box's — with an empty model field, as the 09-04 stamp had",
           limit_active() and limit_until() == float(_t))
    finally:
        os.unlink(_p)
        os.environ.pop("CC_LIMIT_STAMP", None) if _keep is None else os.environ.update({"CC_LIMIT_STAMP": _keep})
    ok("a loop between iterations, with no worker under it, is not wedged", runaway(W(workers=[]), True) == "")
    ok("an expensive job that keeps moving is never a runaway — there is no spend cap anywhere here",
       runaway(W(idle=30), True) == "")
    ok("…and decide() ends it instead of calling it healthy",
       decide(F(status="running", live=True, stop_why="x"))[0][:2] == ("stop", "blocked"))
    ok("a track being ended is not also 'fixed' to running",
       len(decide(F(status="queued", live=True, stop_why="x"))) == 1)
    ok("a session row is never moved by presence, grace, a PR, a worktree, DONE or a runaway — alive, dead past "
       "grace, merged, wedged: decide() has nothing to say; the same facts on a track still decide it",
       all(decide(F(kind="session", **kw)) == [] for kw in (
           dict(status="running"), dict(status="blocked", live=True), dict(status="queued", live=True),
           dict(status="review", pr="u", pr_state="MERGED"), dict(status="running", live=True, stop_why="x"),
           dict(status="running", wt_exists=False, push_err=True), dict(status="running", journal=("DONE", ""))))
       and decide(F(kind="track", status="blocked", live=True))[0][:2] == ("fix", "running")
       and decide(F(status="blocked", live=True))[0][:2] == ("fix", "running"))
    ok("…but a session with a question for the owner is WAITING like a track — the ask record, so it is set, offered "
       "and paged: five course sessions are what waits_for() was written for, and kind=session must not silence them",
       decide(F(kind="session", status="running", live=True, journal=("BLOCKED", "which syllabus?")))[0][:2] == ("ask", "waiting")
       and "which syllabus?" in decide(F(kind="session", status="running", live=True, journal=("BLOCKED", "which syllabus?")))[0][2]
       and decide(F(kind="session", status="running", live=False, journal=("BLOCKED", "which syllabus?")))[0][:2] == ("ask", "waiting")
       and decide(F(kind="session", status="merged", journal=("BLOCKED", "old"))) == [])
    ok("…and it clears the same way once the journal stops saying BLOCKED — never to the `blocked` a dead track "
       "gets. The word it lands on is one the box can SEE: `running` where a session is open, `queued` where the "
       "window is gone, because `running` is a claim that something is happening and nothing is (#174 stopped the "
       "DISPLAY printing it; this is the board field, which was flipped back on every tick of a dead session)",
       decide(F(kind="session", status="waiting", live=True))[0][:2] == ("fix", "running")
       and decide(F(kind="session", status="waiting", live=False))[0][:2] == ("fix", "queued")
       and decide(F(status="waiting", live=False))[0][:2] == ("ask", "blocked"))
    ok("the ONE WORD for a session is its kind, `session` — cc ls and cc digest print that, never the `running` its "
       "row carries — with `waiting` the one track word it wears; a track's word is unchanged",
       effective(F(kind="session", status="running"), []) == "session"
       and effective(F(kind="session", status="waiting"), [("fix", "running", "")]) == "session"
       and effective(F(kind="session", status="running"), [("ask", "waiting", "")]) == "waiting"
       and effective(F(kind="session", status="waiting"), [("fix", "queued", "")]) == "session"   # …and the dead one reads the same
       and effective(F(status="running"), []) == "running" and effective(F(status="waiting"), [("fix", "running", "")]) == "running")

    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tg:
        def g(d, *a):
            return subprocess.run(["git", "-C", d, *a], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
        bare, wt2 = f"{tg}/origin.git", f"{tg}/wt"
        g(tg, "init", "-q", "--bare", bare)
        g(tg, "clone", "-q", bare, wt2)
        g(wt2, "config", "user.email", "s@e"); g(wt2, "config", "user.name", "s")
        open(f"{wt2}/a", "w").write("1")
        g(wt2, "add", "a"); g(wt2, "commit", "-qm", "one")
        ok("real git: a branch origin has never seen cannot be judged — None, so the marker's answer stands",
           branch_unpushed(wt2) is None)
        g(wt2, "push", "-q", "-u", "origin", "HEAD")
        ok("real git: a branch origin HAS is not unpushed, whatever a leftover push.err says",
           branch_unpushed(wt2) is False)
        open(f"{wt2}/a", "w").write("2")
        g(wt2, "commit", "-qam", "two")
        ok("real git: a commit origin does not have IS unpushed", branch_unpushed(wt2) is True)
        ok("real git: a directory that is not a checkout cannot be judged", branch_unpushed(tg + "/nope") is None)

